WEBVTT

00:56.592 --> 00:57.281
Come on.

00:58.123 --> 00:59.059
Come on!

01:09.551 --> 01:11.108
Don't let him get away!

01:24.100 --> 01:29.103
Subtitles by explosiveskull

01:58.041 --> 01:59.375
Get inside now!

01:59.415 --> 02:01.285
Hurry up! You're late!

02:04.121 --> 02:06.189
Proxima's gonna
have your hide.

02:07.505 --> 02:09.032
Get back in the den.

02:11.340 --> 02:12.514
Look what I stole!

02:12.554 --> 02:14.564
Proxima'll give me
an extra portion for this!

02:14.604 --> 02:16.520
Nope, I think she's gonna
give that extra portion to me.

02:16.560 --> 02:17.390
Hey, give it back!

02:17.430 --> 02:18.564
It belongs to
whoever's holding it!

02:18.604 --> 02:19.489
And that's not you!

02:19.529 --> 02:20.724
Lex!

02:21.042 --> 02:22.109
Full Sabacc!

02:22.149 --> 02:23.455
Idiot's Array.

02:23.495 --> 02:24.504
What? Let me see that!

02:24.544 --> 02:25.623
Nope, it's my card.

02:25.663 --> 02:26.675
You cheat.

02:27.575 --> 02:28.409
Han!

02:32.625 --> 02:34.086
You were gone too long!

02:34.148 --> 02:35.595
I knew something
must've gone wrong.

02:35.635 --> 02:37.201
This is nothing.
You should see them.

02:37.241 --> 02:38.277
Look down here!

02:39.681 --> 02:40.710
All right, listen.

02:40.750 --> 02:42.079
I was in the middle
of the exchange,

02:42.119 --> 02:43.241
I'm handing over
the coaxium

02:43.281 --> 02:45.084
and his goons jumped me,
but I showed 'em.

02:45.124 --> 02:45.721
How?

02:45.761 --> 02:47.896
I ran away, then I
boosted their speeder.

02:47.936 --> 02:48.956
What, are we
going somewhere?

02:48.996 --> 02:50.764
Yeah, anywhere we want.

02:51.755 --> 02:54.271
You held on to
one of the vials?

02:54.452 --> 02:55.453
Han's back!

02:57.681 --> 02:59.276
This,
this is worth...

02:59.316 --> 03:00.266
Five, six hundred credits.

03:00.306 --> 03:02.471
That's more than
you said we'd need.

03:02.532 --> 03:04.710
To buy our way out
of the control zone.

03:04.750 --> 03:06.141
And off Corellia.

03:06.181 --> 03:09.249
Han, this could work.

03:09.289 --> 03:10.375
This is gonna work.

03:10.415 --> 03:12.944
Qi'ra, you always said one day
we're gonna get out of here.

03:13.246 --> 03:14.280
This is it.

03:15.699 --> 03:17.101
What are we waiting for?

03:22.233 --> 03:24.662
There he is.
Hey, you two!

03:27.910 --> 03:29.576
Moloch. Hi, how are ya?

03:29.616 --> 03:31.863
I was just on my way
to see Lady Proxima.

03:34.531 --> 03:36.943
What a night I had.

03:37.020 --> 03:39.172
You're not gonna believe it.
You'll believe it, but...

03:40.150 --> 03:42.312
Hold still, scrumrat!

03:43.901 --> 03:44.915
Easy.

03:46.159 --> 03:47.076
Come on.

03:47.116 --> 03:48.204
All right.

03:48.806 --> 03:50.459
Let's go see Lady Proxima.

04:11.258 --> 04:14.046
Well, what happened?

04:14.086 --> 04:15.383
I'll tell you what happened.

04:15.423 --> 04:17.594
They double-crossed you
and tried to kill me.

04:17.634 --> 04:18.431
The money?

04:18.471 --> 04:21.242
- They kept it.
- And my coaxium?

04:21.707 --> 04:22.330
They kept that, too.

04:22.370 --> 04:24.334
But we learned
a very valuable lesson.

04:24.374 --> 04:26.974
We cannot trust those guys.

04:27.014 --> 04:28.840
So you expect me to believe

04:28.925 --> 04:31.476
that you walked away
with nothing!

04:33.119 --> 04:35.764
I ran away with my life.
I think that's something.

04:36.456 --> 04:37.961
To me, that's a lot.

04:38.008 --> 04:40.269
I trusted you
with a simple task,

04:40.309 --> 04:43.044
and all I'm hearing
are excuses.

04:45.664 --> 04:49.373
There must be consequences
for disobedience

04:49.413 --> 04:52.236
or else you never learn.

04:58.420 --> 04:59.367
You know what?

05:01.161 --> 05:02.752
I don't think
I'm ever gonna learn.

05:02.792 --> 05:04.426
What did you say?

05:04.528 --> 05:08.849
I said, next time
somebody hits me,

05:09.538 --> 05:11.289
I hit 'em back.

05:13.971 --> 05:15.389
Moloch, wait!

05:15.613 --> 05:16.756
Don't!

05:16.796 --> 05:19.275
Qi'ra, remember the Silo?

05:19.381 --> 05:21.149
We pulled you
out of that horror,

05:21.189 --> 05:22.691
gave you a home.

05:22.731 --> 05:26.407
Don't throw it away for Han.
He's not worth it!

05:26.447 --> 05:29.898
Whatever he lost on the deal,
we'll earn it back, double.

05:29.938 --> 05:31.225
We will make it up to you.

05:35.474 --> 05:37.774
Everybody, stand back!

05:37.814 --> 05:39.557
What's that supposed to be?

05:39.643 --> 05:41.240
This is a thermal detonator

05:41.280 --> 05:43.775
that I just armed.

05:43.815 --> 05:46.477
- That's a rock!
- No, it's not.

05:46.547 --> 05:47.340
Yes, it is!

05:47.380 --> 05:48.239
And you just made

05:48.279 --> 05:50.002
a clicking sound
with your mouth.

05:50.042 --> 05:51.766
Please tell me
this isn't your plan.

05:51.806 --> 05:53.144
No, this is.

06:03.352 --> 06:04.907
- Get in!
- An M-68?

06:04.947 --> 06:06.747
- Nice, right?
- I love it!

06:14.564 --> 06:16.000
Whoa!

06:39.759 --> 06:42.558
There's a starliner leaving
from Coronet Spaceport,

06:42.598 --> 06:43.833
we're gonna be on it.

06:44.710 --> 06:47.513
We bribe our way through the
checkpoint, and we're free.

06:49.081 --> 06:50.561
I'm gonna be a pilot.

06:50.913 --> 06:52.029
We can get our own ship.

06:52.069 --> 06:53.947
See the galaxy,
all of it.

06:54.935 --> 06:58.763
We won't have to take orders
or be kicked around by anyone.

06:59.182 --> 07:00.183
Ever.

07:03.564 --> 07:05.732
Thought we'd get a little
more of a head start.

07:22.554 --> 07:23.875
- Whoa!
- Hang on!

07:33.520 --> 07:35.203
<i>This is a secure area.</i>

07:35.243 --> 07:37.329
<i>You must have
proper clearance.</i>

07:37.369 --> 07:40.112
<i>Stop at once! You must
follow the proper...</i>

07:41.081 --> 07:42.256
<i>Protocol.</i>

07:45.055 --> 07:46.937
Damn!
That stinger's fast.

07:46.977 --> 07:49.406
Yeah, but we're faster,
right?

07:49.816 --> 07:50.886
I hope so.

08:21.178 --> 08:22.370
<i>Pull over!</i>

08:44.582 --> 08:45.838
Han, no,
we're not gonna make it!

08:45.878 --> 08:46.612
Oh, yeah?

08:46.652 --> 08:48.380
Han, I'm telling you,
it's too tight!

08:48.505 --> 08:49.885
Watch this.

09:13.924 --> 09:14.846
Come on!

09:15.975 --> 09:17.144
We gotta move.

09:28.616 --> 09:30.083
<i>Do not join the line</i>

09:30.151 --> 09:32.881
<i>if you don't have
a boarding pass.</i>

09:32.984 --> 09:36.479
<i>No access without ID chip.</i>

09:36.723 --> 09:39.729
<i>All droids
must be registered.</i>

09:41.178 --> 09:42.848
<i>Move along. Move along.</i>

09:45.332 --> 09:47.391
<i>Stand down. Do not resist!</i>

09:48.555 --> 09:50.117
<i>- Stop struggling.
- Let me go!</i>

09:50.174 --> 09:51.086
<i>Take his arm.</i>

09:51.126 --> 09:51.853
<i>I got him.</i>

09:51.916 --> 09:54.024
<i>Take him to cell 3B.</i>

09:54.064 --> 09:54.865
<i>This way, come on.</i>

09:56.305 --> 09:57.872
<i>Keep moving.
Hold it, hold it.</i>

10:00.216 --> 10:01.351
Next.

10:05.597 --> 10:07.333
Han, they're here.

10:10.231 --> 10:11.007
<i>Hey, what are you...</i>

10:11.047 --> 10:14.073
We're almost there.

10:14.113 --> 10:16.077
- Just hold on to me.
- Next.

10:16.117 --> 10:17.152
Don't look back.

10:18.195 --> 10:20.700
Once we're through,
we've gotta be smart,

10:20.786 --> 10:22.210
figure out
where we're going.

10:22.269 --> 10:24.226
Anywhere the Empire isn't.
Wherever we go,

10:24.272 --> 10:25.738
it can't be worse
than where we've been.

10:25.808 --> 10:29.271
Yes, it can. Out there,
we've got no protection.

10:29.311 --> 10:31.440
We could get snatched up
by traffickers,

10:31.480 --> 10:34.008
sold to Crimson Dawn
or the Hutt Cartel.

10:34.048 --> 10:36.166
That's not gonna happen.

10:36.248 --> 10:37.416
I won't let it.

10:45.125 --> 10:45.760
For luck?

10:47.161 --> 10:48.456
Damn right.

10:52.211 --> 10:53.560
<i>You heard him. Let's go.</i>

10:53.600 --> 10:54.791
Next.

10:57.607 --> 10:59.132
ID chips.

10:59.172 --> 11:01.267
Funny thing,
we don't have 'em.

11:01.707 --> 11:02.629
We have this.

11:02.669 --> 11:04.152
Refined hyperfuel.

11:04.192 --> 11:07.112
It's worth at least
800 credits, maybe more.

11:08.515 --> 11:10.782
You could be detained
just for having that.

11:10.822 --> 11:12.613
What good would
that do anybody?

11:12.838 --> 11:14.683
Let us through,
it's all yours.

11:24.297 --> 11:26.292
The coaxium, now.

11:26.378 --> 11:27.913
As we're going through,
not before.

11:33.245 --> 11:34.446
Do it.

11:36.487 --> 11:37.621
Just do it, do it.

11:41.667 --> 11:44.182
Not so fast, Qi'ra!
Come on!

11:44.254 --> 11:45.841
Wait!
Open the door!

11:45.893 --> 11:48.413
Security! Security,
there has been a breach!

11:48.514 --> 11:49.848
Open the door!

11:50.120 --> 11:52.383
- Run! Run!
- Get your hands off of her!

11:52.603 --> 11:53.657
Run!

11:53.737 --> 11:55.490
Get your hands off of her!

11:56.130 --> 11:57.322
Qi'ra!

11:57.362 --> 11:59.691
Run, Han! Go!

11:59.794 --> 12:01.125
Keep moving.

12:03.212 --> 12:04.495
Qi'ra!

12:04.535 --> 12:05.463
Run!

12:05.503 --> 12:06.888
<i>Traveler
has been apprehended.</i>

12:06.928 --> 12:10.206
Qi'ra, I'll come back!
I'll come back!

12:12.819 --> 12:14.802
<i>All units,
there has been a breach.</i>

12:14.942 --> 12:18.744
<i>Another unauthorized traveler
made it through the gate.</i>

12:18.784 --> 12:20.242
One got through
the gate! Look over there!

12:20.282 --> 12:22.411
<i>Someone
got through the checkpoint.</i>

12:30.148 --> 12:32.445
Keep an eye on that gate.
Yes, sir.

12:32.563 --> 12:33.857
Can't let you through
without a ticket.

12:33.897 --> 12:35.432
Can't let you through
without a ticket.

12:36.397 --> 12:37.948
Hey, wait!

12:38.089 --> 12:39.580
<i>- Hey!
- Come with us.</i>

12:42.108 --> 12:43.764
<i>He's still
out there. Keep looking.</i>

12:56.202 --> 12:57.529
<i>You there, stop!</i>

12:57.569 --> 13:00.180
<i>- Show me some identification.
- Please. Please. No, no!</i>

13:00.230 --> 13:01.410
<i>Do not resist.</i>

13:01.450 --> 13:04.832
<i>Be a part of something.
Join the Empire.</i>

13:04.981 --> 13:09.391
<i>Explore new worlds.
Learn valuable skills.</i>

13:09.456 --> 13:13.219
<i>Bring order and unity
to the galaxy!</i>

13:13.274 --> 13:16.592
<i>Be a part of something.
Join the Empire.</i>

13:17.996 --> 13:19.818
This is where I sign up
to be a pilot, right?

13:19.858 --> 13:21.402
If you apply
for the Imperial Navy,

13:21.442 --> 13:23.236
but most recruits
go into the infantry.

13:23.276 --> 13:26.392
I'm gonna be a pilot.
Best in the galaxy.

13:26.432 --> 13:28.194
You there,
come with us.

13:28.234 --> 13:29.297
Who, me?

13:29.384 --> 13:31.182
We have a few questions
to ask you.

13:31.236 --> 13:32.971
How long
is that gonna take?

13:33.011 --> 13:35.450
Depends on how good you are
at following orders.

13:35.490 --> 13:36.885
Why, have you got
somewhere to be?

13:36.925 --> 13:39.081
Yeah, back here,
as soon as I can.

13:40.206 --> 13:43.535
Don't hear that much.
What's your name, son?

13:43.616 --> 13:44.618
Han.

13:45.001 --> 13:46.368
Han what?

13:48.118 --> 13:49.331
Who are your people?

13:53.113 --> 13:55.883
I don't have people.
I'm alone.

13:57.083 --> 13:58.084
Han...

14:01.097 --> 14:02.218
Solo.

14:03.985 --> 14:05.272
Approved.

14:05.413 --> 14:09.102
Proceed to transport ID 83 for
the Naval Academy at Carida.

14:09.734 --> 14:11.622
Good luck, Han Solo.

14:11.725 --> 14:13.241
We'll have you flying
in no time.

14:26.859 --> 14:30.324
Your Empire needs you.
Troopers forward!

14:30.527 --> 14:32.423
Solo, get up!
We're almost there!

14:32.514 --> 14:34.942
Almost where?
Where are we going?

14:35.013 --> 14:37.893
Just over that last ridge.
Victory is...

14:48.169 --> 14:51.439
My legs! My leg!

15:07.130 --> 15:08.839
<i>Hey, Beckett,
you said we were here</i>

15:08.879 --> 15:10.196
<i>to pull a quick job.</i>

15:10.236 --> 15:12.172
<i>- Yeah.
- Well, this ain't a quick job!</i>

15:12.212 --> 15:13.619
<i>It's a war!</i>

15:14.487 --> 15:16.174
It's always
something with you.

15:17.827 --> 15:20.724
AT-hauler.
That's what we came for.

15:20.764 --> 15:23.141
Forward operations
must be this way.

15:23.181 --> 15:25.810
They are, but the major said
we're supposed to go that way!

15:25.866 --> 15:27.825
Yeah, go that way and die!

15:27.865 --> 15:30.426
That's exactly what happened
to the major!

15:30.563 --> 15:32.768
Who's the ranking
officer now?

15:32.878 --> 15:34.497
You are, Captain.

15:36.509 --> 15:37.946
<i>He's got you there.</i>

15:39.876 --> 15:42.319
So what's the plan,
Captain Beckett?

15:42.399 --> 15:45.670
Val, you take Rio and these
four mud skulls flank left.

15:45.732 --> 15:47.261
I'll take this
mouthy scooch

15:47.372 --> 15:48.516
and we'll go around
to the right

15:48.569 --> 15:50.746
and maybe
we'll get lucky.

15:50.799 --> 15:52.462
<i>Luck's got
nothin' to do with it.</i>

15:53.198 --> 15:55.493
Wait! One question!

15:55.612 --> 15:57.775
- You wanna live, sparky?
- Very much.

15:57.815 --> 16:00.301
Then shut up and do what
your captain tells you.

16:00.930 --> 16:02.591
Let's go!

16:16.875 --> 16:17.628
Captain.

16:17.668 --> 16:19.979
<i>T-15s are down.
We walk from here.</i>

16:20.037 --> 16:21.138
Captain.

16:23.352 --> 16:24.418
I'm Han.

16:25.809 --> 16:27.109
Nobody cares.

16:28.692 --> 16:30.653
Thanks for your help
back there.

16:30.748 --> 16:31.951
You did all right.

16:32.860 --> 16:34.588
I was trained
in aerial combat...

16:34.628 --> 16:36.537
You want some advice?

16:36.610 --> 16:37.804
Get the hell
away from here.

16:37.844 --> 16:40.380
Any way you can,
as fast as you can.

16:43.767 --> 16:44.697
What company
do you command?

16:44.737 --> 16:46.471
None of your business
company.

16:47.003 --> 16:48.378
And we're full up.

16:49.354 --> 16:50.770
<i>Stick
to soldiering, kid.</i>

16:50.850 --> 16:52.251
<i>You don't want
any part of this.</i>

16:58.855 --> 17:00.090
<i>Hang on, guys!</i>

17:02.288 --> 17:03.659
Attention!

17:04.059 --> 17:06.960
In three hours, we move out
for the southern marshlands.

17:07.021 --> 17:09.618
I want an advance party
of ten men.

17:09.697 --> 17:11.499
Great, more mud.

17:11.570 --> 17:13.698
What was that?

17:13.832 --> 17:16.547
Just wondering what our
objective is, Lieutenant.

17:16.611 --> 17:19.408
Bring peace and prosperity
to the galaxy,

17:19.495 --> 17:21.400
install a regime
loyal to the Emperor,

17:21.440 --> 17:23.445
and eradicate
the hostiles.

17:23.527 --> 17:25.741
It's their planet,
we're the hostiles.

17:26.229 --> 17:27.993
You got a problem, trooper?

17:29.181 --> 17:30.549
No problem, sir.

17:33.299 --> 17:34.527
Moving out.

17:34.786 --> 17:37.424
To the southern
marshlands! Move out!

17:37.515 --> 17:39.483
You heard 'em!
Let's move out!

17:47.982 --> 17:49.716
Mmm. Looks like
they're running sorties

17:49.756 --> 17:51.343
every 30 minutes.

17:51.413 --> 17:53.853
Yeah, I can take out the
guards at the perimeter,

17:53.893 --> 17:55.208
signalman, pilot.

17:55.248 --> 17:56.697
Hell, I'll just
take 'em all out.

17:56.823 --> 17:58.125
What are we
looking at?

18:01.739 --> 18:03.703
You have a talent for
sticking your nose in

18:03.743 --> 18:05.150
where it doesn't belong.

18:05.190 --> 18:06.752
I just couldn't help
but notice

18:06.792 --> 18:09.062
you're wearing a uniform
pock-full of laser burns.

18:09.102 --> 18:11.613
So either
you heal real quick

18:11.691 --> 18:13.800
or you stole it off
a dead man.

18:13.840 --> 18:15.975
You're not Imperial Army.

18:16.063 --> 18:17.482
You're thieves here
to steal equipment

18:17.522 --> 18:19.349
for a job and I want in.

18:19.841 --> 18:21.777
- Well, now we gotta shoot him.
- No.

18:22.741 --> 18:24.878
Snap his neck.
It's less mess.

18:24.952 --> 18:26.292
Or you take me with you.

18:26.332 --> 18:29.044
Look, I came up running scams
on the streets of Corellia.

18:29.153 --> 18:31.548
I was boosting AV-21s
when I was ten.

18:31.588 --> 18:33.428
I'm a driver, a flyer,

18:33.492 --> 18:36.918
and hey, you said yourself.
I gotta get outta here. Right?

18:36.974 --> 18:39.486
<i>What's a fancy flyboy
doing down in the mud?</i>

18:40.638 --> 18:42.753
I got kicked out
of the Imperial Academy

18:42.836 --> 18:44.346
for having
a mind of my own.

18:44.448 --> 18:47.865
But I am a great pilot.
And I gotta get home.

18:47.933 --> 18:50.504
<i>This guy is nuts. No one
goes back to Corellia.</i>

18:50.561 --> 18:52.000
I got a reason.

18:52.070 --> 18:54.164
We've already
got a great pilot.

18:54.345 --> 18:56.793
The Ardennian.

18:56.833 --> 18:58.965
<i>Ardennian?
You got a lot of nerve, pal.</i>

18:59.035 --> 19:00.428
<i>I'm an Imperial trooper.</i>

19:00.491 --> 19:01.671
Oh, really?
A couple of your arms

19:01.711 --> 19:02.524
popped out of your butt

19:02.564 --> 19:04.294
and hiked up your pants,
trooper.

19:04.334 --> 19:05.093
<i>Oh, yeah?</i>

19:05.133 --> 19:07.536
Look, I'll do whatever it
takes to get back to Corellia.

19:07.576 --> 19:08.796
I've already been away
too long.

19:08.836 --> 19:10.755
Just give me a shot.

19:11.272 --> 19:12.499
<i>Whoa. Hold it.</i>

19:14.519 --> 19:15.985
Well, if you're
not interested in me,

19:16.025 --> 19:19.021
I think the lieutenant might
be very interested in you.

19:22.793 --> 19:24.095
Blackmail.

19:26.531 --> 19:27.499
Lieutenant.

19:27.539 --> 19:28.521
Captain.

19:29.533 --> 19:32.078
Lieutenant, we have
apprehended a deserter.

19:32.118 --> 19:33.026
Take him.

19:33.066 --> 19:33.857
Wait.

19:33.897 --> 19:36.865
I should've known.
This one's a troublemaker.

19:36.905 --> 19:39.098
And a liar. Don't
believe anything he says.

19:39.138 --> 19:41.235
<i>- Don't go anywhere without me.
- All right, let's go.</i>

19:41.290 --> 19:42.514
Feed him to the beast.

19:42.558 --> 19:44.240
The beast?
Wait, there's a beast?

19:44.281 --> 19:45.489
<i>- Hold on!
- Move it!</i>

19:45.529 --> 19:47.745
Listen, that guy's not
even an officer. All right?

19:47.785 --> 19:49.043
<i>- He was lying!
- Quiet!</i>

19:50.914 --> 19:51.915
<i>Don't care.</i>

19:54.791 --> 19:56.558
<i>Haven't fed him
in three days.</i>

19:56.598 --> 19:57.796
<i>Should be fun.</i>

20:44.398 --> 20:46.794
Oh! Hey!
Hey, big fella.

20:46.834 --> 20:49.542
Just calm down.
Take it easy.

20:49.652 --> 20:51.136
We're on the same side.

20:51.231 --> 20:52.890
You like treats?

20:54.469 --> 20:56.940
Help!
Let me out of here!

20:56.980 --> 20:58.149
Let me out of here!

21:01.652 --> 21:03.289
A-ha! Gotcha!

21:09.463 --> 21:10.700
Ahhh!

21:24.190 --> 21:25.983
<i>Ah, this was
just getting good.</i>

21:26.023 --> 21:27.370
<i>- He killed him too fast.
- Yeah!</i>

21:27.410 --> 21:28.710
<i>Kill him slower.</i>

21:31.504 --> 21:32.951
Wait, wait, wait, wait!

21:32.991 --> 21:35.553
Wait! Wait!

21:39.288 --> 21:40.395
Yeah, I speak a little.

21:40.435 --> 21:43.353
Now just listen to me, you...

22:02.009 --> 22:03.728
Yes, yes!

22:04.401 --> 22:05.637
No, no, no, no!

22:08.469 --> 22:09.470
Do it!

22:09.652 --> 22:10.756
Come on.

22:12.432 --> 22:14.126
Oh, no!

22:14.487 --> 22:16.306
<i>Ten credits, he doesn't
last another minute.</i>

22:16.378 --> 22:18.206
Let me out of here!

22:18.325 --> 22:20.002
I can't take it anymore!

22:21.154 --> 22:23.245
<i>- Oh, no! Stop, please!
- That's it. Get him!</i>

22:24.054 --> 22:28.001
You tired, you mangy
Kashyyykian moof-milker?

22:39.208 --> 22:41.757
See what happens
when you listen to me?

22:41.797 --> 22:43.743
Hey, what are you doing?

22:46.119 --> 22:47.787
Ow.

22:50.961 --> 22:51.961
Follow me!

23:03.016 --> 23:04.264
Wait, wait.

23:04.304 --> 23:06.198
Come here.
Listen to me.

23:06.238 --> 23:07.196
You don't understand,
okay?

23:07.236 --> 23:08.137
I have some
very good friends

23:08.177 --> 23:09.281
waiting for me
at that airfield.

23:09.321 --> 23:10.718
They're leaving
right now.

23:10.758 --> 23:12.437
That's our one way
off this mud ball.

23:12.477 --> 23:14.112
If you wanna live,
we go that way.

23:14.152 --> 23:16.624
After that, you go whichever
way you want, I don't care!

23:16.664 --> 23:18.772
But right now,
that's the way you go!

23:21.200 --> 23:22.535
Trust me!

23:23.139 --> 23:25.497
Val, let's go!

23:28.821 --> 23:31.734
How do they breathe in these
suits? It's so stuffy!

23:31.992 --> 23:33.689
No wonder
they're such lousy pilots.

23:33.729 --> 23:35.405
You can't turn your head,
you can't breathe,

23:35.445 --> 23:36.834
you can't hear each other!

23:43.771 --> 23:45.277
I'll be damned.

23:45.371 --> 23:46.781
Hey, look who's back!

23:46.854 --> 23:48.095
Unbelievable!

23:48.189 --> 23:49.907
Wait!

23:49.947 --> 23:51.804
Wait!

23:51.851 --> 23:54.477
Whoa, is that a Wookiee?
Incredible!

23:54.517 --> 23:55.841
I'll say it, I don't care.

23:55.920 --> 23:57.415
This kid's growing on me.

23:57.588 --> 23:59.388
Wait!

24:03.294 --> 24:04.040
You know, we could always use

24:04.080 --> 24:06.095
some muscle
on a job like this.

24:06.329 --> 24:08.114
Don't even
think about it!

24:08.190 --> 24:10.548
I'm telling you, you will
never have a deeper sleep

24:10.588 --> 24:12.313
than curled up
in a Wookiee's lap.

24:18.174 --> 24:20.930
I told you!

24:20.970 --> 24:23.057
Very good friends!

24:48.250 --> 24:50.685
We couldn't have done this
maybe, like, one at a time?

25:18.856 --> 25:20.590
Thanks for helping me
get outta there.

25:26.945 --> 25:28.879
No, they only took you
because of me.

25:30.059 --> 25:31.201
Hey!

25:31.321 --> 25:33.952
I got us
a real sweet deal here.

25:34.047 --> 25:36.006
We do this one job
with them,

25:36.115 --> 25:37.910
we make some real money,

25:38.104 --> 25:40.112
and then we're free.

25:40.396 --> 25:42.263
When's the last time
you could say that?

25:45.700 --> 25:47.970
Been a while
for me, too.

25:49.397 --> 25:51.694
So what's your name,
anyway?

25:55.036 --> 25:57.463
Chewbacca?

25:57.559 --> 25:59.847
All right, well, you're gonna
need a nickname,

25:59.926 --> 26:01.661
'cause I ain't saying that
every time.

26:07.471 --> 26:08.922
Here it comes.
Take a look.

26:08.962 --> 26:09.604
Yeah.

26:09.644 --> 26:13.539
We hit the Conveyex between
the tower and the bridge.

26:13.601 --> 26:16.780
Rio drops us in, we separate
the payload container,

26:16.820 --> 26:19.410
cable it up to the AT-hauler
and then...

26:19.451 --> 26:21.304
Rio jams
their distress signal.

26:21.986 --> 26:23.086
I blow the bridge,

26:23.126 --> 26:25.019
the container slides
right off the track

26:25.059 --> 26:26.473
and we sail away.

26:26.513 --> 26:28.276
You trip that security beam,

26:28.316 --> 26:29.439
wake up those Vipers,

26:29.479 --> 26:31.901
it's liable to get
real spicy, real fast.

26:31.963 --> 26:34.083
Well, I'm not the one
you should be worried about.

26:34.201 --> 26:35.583
Enfys Nest.

26:35.677 --> 26:37.041
What's an Enfys Nest?

26:37.117 --> 26:38.212
I told you,
we're way ahead

26:38.252 --> 26:40.035
of the competition
on this one.

26:40.097 --> 26:41.293
There's no way Enfys Nest

26:41.333 --> 26:43.395
even knows
about this shipment.

26:43.561 --> 26:45.158
Only my guy
has the intel.

26:45.198 --> 26:47.687
Well, you better
be right. Yeah?

26:47.763 --> 26:49.900
Because sometimes,
you put your faith

26:49.990 --> 26:51.324
in the wrong people.

26:53.559 --> 26:56.049
<i>Our whole future
depends on this one score</i>

26:56.089 --> 26:57.407
<i>and you bring in amateurs.</i>

26:57.462 --> 26:58.689
<i>In case you hadn't noticed,</i>

26:58.729 --> 27:00.371
<i>we're a little shorthanded.</i>

27:00.441 --> 27:01.895
So we get who we need.

27:01.966 --> 27:04.423
The Xan sisters, or Bossk.

27:04.483 --> 27:06.753
But, no, instead you're
putting our lives

27:06.793 --> 27:08.369
in the hands of morons.

27:09.412 --> 27:10.740
You guys morons?

27:10.819 --> 27:11.631
No!

27:11.671 --> 27:13.817
- No. See?
- We're not morons.

27:13.857 --> 27:16.831
Look, I waited a long time
for a shot like this.

27:16.871 --> 27:18.677
I'm not about to screw it up,
all right?

27:19.507 --> 27:20.636
Oh, come on, Val!

27:20.708 --> 27:22.313
He looks so sincere.

27:22.360 --> 27:23.723
Plus, have you ever
tried to disinvite

27:23.763 --> 27:24.859
a Wookiee to anything?

27:24.899 --> 27:27.429
Not a good idea!

27:27.510 --> 27:28.819
This is not funny!

27:28.984 --> 27:33.348
Look, now, I have great
instincts about these guys.

27:33.672 --> 27:37.260
And, besides,
do you see any other options?

27:37.300 --> 27:38.648
I just hope you know
what you're doing.

27:38.688 --> 27:41.452
Yeah, I know exactly
what I'm doing and why.

27:41.518 --> 27:43.344
We're gonna
clear our debts,

27:43.384 --> 27:45.297
go back to Glee Anselm,

27:46.253 --> 27:49.016
and I'm finally gonna learn
how to play that valachord.

27:49.056 --> 27:51.228
Babe, you're never gonna learn
how to play the valachord.

27:51.268 --> 27:53.096
She's right.
You are tone-deaf.

27:56.661 --> 27:59.028
So what's your sob story,
flyboy?

27:59.068 --> 27:59.942
Who, me?

27:59.982 --> 28:01.978
You're after something,
I know the look.

28:02.018 --> 28:03.674
What is it?
Revenge?

28:04.648 --> 28:06.145
No, it's not revenge.

28:06.411 --> 28:07.739
Look at him.

28:07.865 --> 28:09.426
If it's anything,
it's a girl.

28:09.466 --> 28:10.447
Oh, a girl!

28:10.487 --> 28:13.053
Tell us about the girl, Han.
Is she nice?

28:13.648 --> 28:15.312
Does she have sharp teeth?

28:18.592 --> 28:19.794
There was a girl.

28:20.143 --> 28:23.431
But I got out,
she didn't.

28:25.352 --> 28:28.149
I swore to myself
I'd become a pilot,

28:28.471 --> 28:30.236
get a ship,

28:30.341 --> 28:31.623
go back and find her.

28:32.760 --> 28:36.518
That's what I'm gonna do
right after this job.

28:36.589 --> 28:38.624
How you know
she'll still be there?

28:39.522 --> 28:41.147
I just know.

28:41.225 --> 28:42.565
Personally, I refuse
to be tied down

28:42.605 --> 28:44.766
by anyone,
though many have tried.

28:44.806 --> 28:47.636
Come on, Rio.
You don't fool me.

28:47.775 --> 28:49.489
Everybody needs somebody.

28:50.467 --> 28:54.003
Even a broken down
old crook like this one.

29:04.864 --> 29:06.714
How about you? What are you
gonna do with your share?

29:19.683 --> 29:20.959
What was he saying?

29:20.999 --> 29:22.403
He said the Wookiees
were enslaved

29:22.443 --> 29:24.976
by the Empire,
taken off Kashyyyk.

29:25.147 --> 29:26.991
He's searching
for his, uh...

29:28.303 --> 29:30.438
I don't know if he said
tribe or family.

29:31.778 --> 29:33.086
What's the difference?

29:36.213 --> 29:37.709
Show me how to do that.

29:37.891 --> 29:40.118
The only thing
you need to learn to do

29:42.669 --> 29:45.441
is do what I say
when I say it.

29:45.698 --> 29:47.527
And this time tomorrow,

29:47.567 --> 29:48.802
you'll have
more than enough

29:48.842 --> 29:50.244
to buy your own ship.

30:11.969 --> 30:13.491
<i>Starting the clock.</i>

30:13.531 --> 30:16.232
Jamming their signal.
9.6 to the bridge.

30:16.272 --> 30:18.676
<i>Let's find out how good
we really are, folks.</i>

30:30.360 --> 30:31.275
I'm fine!

30:35.576 --> 30:37.259
Val, how's it going
up there?

30:41.434 --> 30:42.569
Never better.

31:05.729 --> 31:07.132
Coaxium.

31:07.514 --> 31:09.456
Enough to power a fleet!

31:09.496 --> 31:12.002
Or blow us all
straight to hell!

31:14.630 --> 31:15.964
<i>All right, talk to me.</i>

31:16.185 --> 31:17.413
Is it a good day?

31:17.624 --> 31:19.219
<i>It's a great day!</i>

31:19.259 --> 31:21.822
Best day of your life,
my grabby friend!

31:21.892 --> 31:23.019
I don't know,
you've never been

31:23.059 --> 31:24.848
to a Mynock roast
on Ardennia.

31:24.888 --> 31:25.990
It's nuts!

31:28.612 --> 31:29.806
Here they come!

31:29.901 --> 31:31.595
Get down to the couplers!

31:31.643 --> 31:33.196
Rio, fall back!

31:33.236 --> 31:34.573
Well, that didn't
take 'em long.

31:52.882 --> 31:53.851
Chewie!

32:10.185 --> 32:11.948
You all right?

32:11.988 --> 32:13.789
Little close there,
buddy!

32:18.209 --> 32:19.920
Han, what's the holdup?

32:20.764 --> 32:22.040
All right, together.

32:24.531 --> 32:25.858
Now!

32:30.881 --> 32:32.850
All right!

32:33.644 --> 32:34.644
Oh!

32:38.751 --> 32:41.192
They got one uncoupled.
Where are you, buddy?

32:41.265 --> 32:43.096
<i>Just up here
planning my retirement.</i>

32:43.098 --> 32:44.384
Thinking about opening
a cantina

32:44.386 --> 32:46.756
somewhere warm
but not too warm, you know?

32:46.830 --> 32:49.167
Lowering
the winch cables now!

33:05.897 --> 33:07.960
I knew it! I told him!
Beckett!

33:08.034 --> 33:09.202
<i>He's coming!</i>

33:10.715 --> 33:13.245
Damn it! I'm never gonna
hear the end of this!

33:17.993 --> 33:19.221
Who's that?

33:19.354 --> 33:20.815
Enfys Nest!

33:20.817 --> 33:22.608
Marauders, pirates.

33:22.610 --> 33:24.440
Come to snake the score
from under us.

33:25.468 --> 33:27.203
<i>Ready your harpoons.</i>

33:27.205 --> 33:28.206
<i>Move in.</i>

34:08.708 --> 34:11.103
Hang on!
I got an uninvited guest.

34:11.189 --> 34:14.547
Get off of my ship!

34:18.732 --> 34:20.614
You still with us, brother?

34:20.670 --> 34:22.571
Yeah, I'm okay.

34:22.629 --> 34:24.631
Just nicked one of my shoulders.
It's nothing.

34:25.212 --> 34:26.406
He's not okay.

34:33.643 --> 34:35.027
Chewie!

34:35.119 --> 34:37.395
You gotta uncouple this one
on your own!

34:42.842 --> 34:44.168
Han!

34:44.318 --> 34:45.485
I'm on it!

34:55.613 --> 34:56.187
Val!

34:56.189 --> 34:59.179
<i>Keep your eyes open.
We just tripped a sensor.</i>

35:04.660 --> 35:06.227
Viper droids
headed your way!

35:07.369 --> 35:09.397
Rio?

35:09.593 --> 35:11.612
Yeah, it looks worse
than it is.

35:12.169 --> 35:14.364
Just gotta patch it up.

35:14.404 --> 35:16.772
Maybe rest my eyes
for a minute.

35:36.967 --> 35:38.943
<i>Enough!
I'm going in.</i>

36:04.313 --> 36:05.648
You weren't lying, kid.

36:06.989 --> 36:08.684
You're a hell of a pilot.

36:08.724 --> 36:10.079
Rio, stay with me, buddy.

36:23.074 --> 36:25.021
Beckett,
we just lost a cable!

36:26.136 --> 36:28.007
<i>2.1 to the bridge!</i>

36:32.078 --> 36:33.744
It's no good
to die alone, kid.

36:35.489 --> 36:36.750
Val was right.

36:39.387 --> 36:40.515
Rio?

37:11.322 --> 37:13.011
Beckett, we're .8
from the bridge!

37:13.052 --> 37:15.214
<i>Val's still on the track!</i>

37:15.254 --> 37:17.452
Val, you gotta
get off that bridge!

37:17.454 --> 37:18.355
We're here!

37:22.870 --> 37:24.557
They got me pinned!

37:24.627 --> 37:26.778
I'm gonna have to finish
the job from right here.

37:26.933 --> 37:28.420
What?

37:28.497 --> 37:30.099
It's been a ride, babe.

37:31.703 --> 37:33.671
And I wouldn't trade it
for anything.

37:34.478 --> 37:35.397
<i>Val!</i>

37:35.467 --> 37:36.668
No!

37:42.114 --> 37:44.547
No!

37:58.129 --> 38:00.004
Chewie, now!

38:22.323 --> 38:24.551
<i>Beckett, I can't
pull it away from 'em.</i>

38:25.288 --> 38:27.689
They'll let go,
you fly straight!

38:29.963 --> 38:31.556
<i>Release your cables</i>

38:31.731 --> 38:33.032
<i>or die!</i>

38:34.305 --> 38:35.019
We're too close.

38:35.021 --> 38:36.149
I gotta release.

38:36.151 --> 38:37.625
You do what
I tell you, Han!

38:37.627 --> 38:39.078
Chewie, grab the line!

38:39.168 --> 38:40.509
Don't you do it!

38:43.805 --> 38:45.001
Han!

38:45.041 --> 38:46.607
<i>You coward!</i>

39:35.223 --> 39:36.707
What the hell?

39:36.998 --> 39:40.439
You don't listen
and you can't follow orders!

39:40.565 --> 39:42.907
You have any idea
what you've done?

39:43.024 --> 39:45.811
We were not stealing
for ourselves,

39:45.813 --> 39:48.427
we were hired
by Crimson Dawn.

39:50.788 --> 39:53.050
Crimson Dawn?

39:53.052 --> 39:55.409
Now we owe them 100 keys
of refined coaxium.

39:55.411 --> 39:57.607
When they find out
we don't got it,

39:57.910 --> 39:59.677
they're gonna kill us.

40:00.744 --> 40:02.372
Right.

40:02.616 --> 40:03.797
We run.

40:03.844 --> 40:06.707
I'm already a deserter.
What's the difference?

40:07.020 --> 40:08.047
The difference

40:08.049 --> 40:09.706
is the Empire
doesn't send out

40:09.708 --> 40:12.042
a team of enforcers
to hunt you down

40:12.125 --> 40:13.564
when you're a deserter.

40:13.643 --> 40:15.076
Dryden Vos will.

40:17.151 --> 40:18.171
You have any idea
what it's like

40:18.173 --> 40:20.110
to live with a price
on your head?

40:21.690 --> 40:24.359
The only thing to do
is to go to them.

40:24.446 --> 40:26.816
Maybe I can find some way
to make it up to him.

40:31.380 --> 40:32.814
Then that's what we do.

40:37.621 --> 40:38.821
No.

40:42.986 --> 40:45.323
He knows me,
not you.

40:46.332 --> 40:48.667
If you come with me

40:49.316 --> 40:51.611
and show your face,

40:51.613 --> 40:53.447
if they don't kill you,

40:55.001 --> 40:57.105
you're in this life for good.

40:59.360 --> 41:02.195
You find some way
to square this,

41:04.139 --> 41:05.975
we still get our money?

41:07.783 --> 41:09.183
Maybe.

41:11.665 --> 41:14.001
For me,
it's worth the risk.

41:16.663 --> 41:17.663
How about you?

41:24.837 --> 41:26.505
That's yes.

41:28.385 --> 41:31.615
Sorry I punched your face.

41:31.834 --> 41:34.003
Happens more often
than you think.

41:36.138 --> 41:37.024
So when we get up there,

41:37.026 --> 41:39.303
Dryden Vos is waiting for us
at Fort Ypso?

41:39.383 --> 41:42.462
Nearby,
on his yacht.

41:42.528 --> 41:44.522
You're gonna know
how to find it?

41:44.601 --> 41:46.171
That won't be
a problem.

42:27.518 --> 42:30.121
I'll need to
check your weapons.

42:31.488 --> 42:32.967
That's all I got left.

43:13.475 --> 43:16.367
I'm here to see Dryden.
He's expecting me.

43:16.474 --> 43:17.797
He'll be with you
shortly.

43:17.799 --> 43:19.962
He's just finishing
with the regional governor.

43:25.215 --> 43:26.479
Excuse me, sir.

43:26.481 --> 43:27.543
Yes.

43:27.632 --> 43:30.519
- Beckett has arrived.
- Oh.

43:32.642 --> 43:36.221
Put this in my office.
I might be needing it later.

43:42.676 --> 43:45.205
I get all worked up.
Silly.

43:45.480 --> 43:46.780
It's a party.

43:50.238 --> 43:51.408
Hey.

43:51.410 --> 43:54.568
These people are
not your friends

43:54.694 --> 43:57.325
and they're never gonna be,
so don't talk to any of 'em.

43:57.397 --> 43:58.526
Don't look at anybody,

43:58.528 --> 44:00.355
just keep your eyes down.

44:04.149 --> 44:05.702
I might get a drink.

44:18.488 --> 44:19.963
No, yeah, whatever.

44:38.319 --> 44:40.787
Chewie, would you please...

44:49.903 --> 44:51.664
Qi'ra, what are you
doing here?

44:51.666 --> 44:53.028
I work here.

44:53.303 --> 44:55.064
What's your excuse?

44:55.066 --> 44:56.395
My... I...

44:56.397 --> 44:58.067
Qi'ra, I was...

45:00.673 --> 45:02.775
I was coming back
for you.

45:03.457 --> 45:05.300
It's in the past, Han.

45:05.388 --> 45:05.927
Not for me.

45:05.967 --> 45:06.893
The only reason I'm here,

45:06.895 --> 45:08.497
I was doing this job,
get a little money

45:08.548 --> 45:11.238
and then I was gonna come back
to Corellia and find you.

45:11.315 --> 45:13.383
Well, now you don't have to.

45:14.414 --> 45:16.382
I'm right in front of you.

45:18.599 --> 45:19.891
That day...

45:19.946 --> 45:21.641
Sometimes,
a lot of times, I think...

45:21.643 --> 45:22.944
If you'd have stayed,

45:24.156 --> 45:26.226
they would've killed you.

45:27.651 --> 45:29.652
I'm glad you got out.

45:33.992 --> 45:35.393
How did you get out?

45:39.156 --> 45:41.025
I didn't.

45:44.227 --> 45:45.981
You look good.

45:46.003 --> 45:47.763
A little rough
around the edges,

45:47.860 --> 45:49.162
but good.

45:49.705 --> 45:50.808
You too.

45:51.547 --> 45:52.743
Thank you, Ottilie.

45:53.578 --> 45:55.375
Have you been attentive
to Dok-Ondar?

45:55.377 --> 45:56.445
Very.

45:59.893 --> 46:01.922
What should we drink to?

46:02.300 --> 46:05.170
Let's drink two
and see where it goes.

46:13.181 --> 46:15.864
Did you ever get that ship
we were going to fly away on?

46:15.887 --> 46:18.050
Yeah.
Sort of.

46:18.119 --> 46:20.402
About to.
That's why I'm here.

46:20.461 --> 46:22.778
I'm working on a...

46:22.780 --> 46:24.737
Very big deal.

46:24.764 --> 46:25.891
How big?

46:26.081 --> 46:27.091
Enormous.

46:27.146 --> 46:30.676
Really? And when are you going
to close this enormous deal?

46:30.791 --> 46:32.359
Any minute.

46:33.743 --> 46:36.041
I thought
about you a lot.

46:36.102 --> 46:39.317
Off somewhere,
some adventure.

46:39.411 --> 46:42.448
I imagined myself with you.
It always made me...

46:45.449 --> 46:47.179
- What?
- Hey.

46:47.305 --> 46:49.301
What did I say?

46:49.355 --> 46:51.394
Look, I can't keep my eyes
down the whole time.

46:51.474 --> 46:52.870
I'm gonna
bump into something.

46:52.912 --> 46:54.209
But I told you
not to talk to anyone.

46:54.276 --> 46:55.277
Beckett.

46:56.164 --> 46:59.034
Wait.
You two work together?

47:00.139 --> 47:01.408
- Yeah.
- Tobias!

47:03.320 --> 47:05.047
Dryden.

47:05.096 --> 47:07.103
Are you all right?
Are you hurt?

47:07.105 --> 47:08.973
No, I'm fine.

47:09.997 --> 47:11.692
I'm sorry
to hear about Val.

47:11.787 --> 47:13.148
Yeah,
I appreciate that.

47:13.225 --> 47:14.492
But there was no way
we could've anticipated...

47:14.494 --> 47:17.054
I don't believe
we've been introduced.

47:17.056 --> 47:20.105
Yeah. This is Han Solo
and Chewbacca.

47:20.107 --> 47:21.701
They're with me.

47:21.703 --> 47:23.431
I'm Dryden Vos.

47:23.712 --> 47:27.293
I see you've already met
my top lieutenant.

47:29.729 --> 47:31.908
Han and I grew up
together on Corellia.

47:32.594 --> 47:35.001
Oh, fellow scrumrat.

47:35.099 --> 47:38.431
I admire anyone who can crawl
their way out of the sewer.

47:38.564 --> 47:41.347
Especially,
a sewer as putrid as Corellia.

47:41.417 --> 47:43.411
The stench, am I right?

47:44.550 --> 47:46.049
Well, it's good
to have you.

47:46.224 --> 47:47.959
Welcome.

47:48.007 --> 47:50.341
And you, too, Chewbacca,
welcome.

47:51.004 --> 47:55.040
All right, let's eat a
little, drink a lot,

47:55.042 --> 47:56.385
and talk privately.

47:59.581 --> 48:00.989
We're just friends,
all right?

48:00.991 --> 48:02.917
You're touchy.

48:03.805 --> 48:07.477
Beckett, you have
put me in a terrible position.

48:07.528 --> 48:09.608
I know, Dryden,
and I am sorry.

48:09.667 --> 48:10.592
You're sorry?

48:10.630 --> 48:12.092
Dryden, there were
complications.

48:12.094 --> 48:12.883
There were factors.

48:12.885 --> 48:16.305
Enfys Nest has been
a constant irritation forever.

48:16.307 --> 48:17.913
It's one you should've
anticipated,

48:17.915 --> 48:19.476
it's one you should've
dealt with.

48:19.478 --> 48:20.964
Trust me, I know
I made a mistake,

48:21.033 --> 48:23.955
but when you hired me,
you told me

48:23.957 --> 48:24.955
no one else
had this information...

48:24.957 --> 48:26.346
Test me!

48:27.417 --> 48:30.314
Test me one more time,
you'll see what happens.

48:30.386 --> 48:32.773
I think what Dryden
is trying to say

48:32.775 --> 48:35.706
is that we're not interested
in why you don't have it.

48:35.913 --> 48:37.767
No, I'm not interested.

48:37.769 --> 48:39.577
I'm not interested
at all.

48:39.766 --> 48:40.838
Dryden,

48:40.840 --> 48:42.814
what can I do
to make this right?

48:42.894 --> 48:44.722
"Make this right?"

48:44.994 --> 48:47.189
There is no
making this right.

48:47.433 --> 48:48.719
You know who I answer to

48:48.721 --> 48:51.074
and you know
what he'll expect of me.

48:51.076 --> 48:53.212
He'll say, "There have
to be consequences."

48:53.214 --> 48:56.938
So here's what I need you
to do for me.

48:57.066 --> 49:00.600
I need you to give me
a reason

49:01.062 --> 49:03.706
not to kill you all.

49:03.755 --> 49:05.666
Because I will
make it up to you.

49:05.668 --> 49:06.945
No, no, no. How?

49:06.947 --> 49:08.231
How will you
make it up to me?

49:08.233 --> 49:11.632
By delivering exactly
what was promised.

49:12.444 --> 49:15.298
100 k-grams of
refined coaxium?

49:15.300 --> 49:18.734
Yes. We will simply steal it
from somewhere else.

49:18.736 --> 49:20.165
From where?

49:20.246 --> 49:21.375
You'll be hard pushed
to find that

49:21.377 --> 49:23.051
anywhere outside
an Imperial vault.

49:23.053 --> 49:25.048
Scarif.
Maybe Mercy Island.

49:25.050 --> 49:26.384
That's impossible.

49:26.386 --> 49:29.082
So, let's come up
with some other options.

49:29.149 --> 49:30.444
Other ideas
that we might...

49:30.446 --> 49:32.349
What about unrefined?

49:35.504 --> 49:38.555
Well, the only known
source of astatic coaxium

49:38.602 --> 49:41.550
is a fissure vent beneath
the spice mines on Kessel.

49:41.552 --> 49:43.785
Yeah. That's the one
I was thinking of.

49:43.787 --> 49:45.417
That's a very,
very good one.

49:45.496 --> 49:47.709
But see,
the Pykes control Kessel.

49:47.762 --> 49:48.784
Crimson Dawn maintains

49:48.826 --> 49:51.121
a fragile alliance
with the Pykes.

49:51.210 --> 49:53.486
It's one that
I can't jeopardize

49:53.488 --> 49:55.616
without risking an all-out
war with the Syndicates,

49:55.618 --> 49:58.795
and that, gentlemen,
I will not do.

49:58.984 --> 50:02.590
So, if that's all you have,
I think we're done here.

50:02.592 --> 50:03.452
Not all we have.

50:03.454 --> 50:06.484
We don't have any alliance
with the Pykes.

50:06.486 --> 50:08.954
Right, so nobody is gonna know
we're working for you.

50:18.940 --> 50:19.940
Possible?

50:20.405 --> 50:21.667
It's risky.

50:21.669 --> 50:24.366
As soon as the raw coaxium
is removed from the vault,

50:24.368 --> 50:26.021
it starts to destabilize,

50:26.023 --> 50:27.656
so unless...

50:27.658 --> 50:29.187
Unless...

50:29.518 --> 50:30.785
Unless...

50:31.411 --> 50:32.539
Work with me here.

50:32.541 --> 50:34.327
Unless you could
find somewhere

50:34.329 --> 50:36.029
to get it processed fast.

50:36.031 --> 50:37.313
- Uh...
- Uh...

50:38.220 --> 50:39.521
Well...

50:40.511 --> 50:41.874
He's saying Savareen?

50:42.093 --> 50:43.225
Savareen.

50:43.227 --> 50:45.132
Yeah,
it's an old refinery there

50:45.134 --> 50:47.315
and it's not under
Imperial jurisdiction.

50:47.401 --> 50:49.058
But Qi'ra's right.

50:49.120 --> 50:52.550
The canisters will explode
before you get there,

50:52.552 --> 50:54.932
so you'd need
an incredibly fast ship

50:54.988 --> 50:56.641
and a brilliant pilot.

50:56.755 --> 50:58.289
We'll find a ship.

50:58.291 --> 51:00.001
We've already
got the pilot.

51:04.686 --> 51:08.449
He is arrogant
and he's hungry.

51:08.480 --> 51:09.435
So what do you think,
my dear?

51:09.437 --> 51:14.235
You think your friend here
can do what needs to be done?

51:20.758 --> 51:22.726
Yes, I believe he can.

51:24.340 --> 51:25.628
Well, that is good news,

51:25.630 --> 51:27.625
because you're going with him

51:27.920 --> 51:30.191
to see that he does.

51:31.541 --> 51:33.408
All right?

51:34.634 --> 51:35.636
Of course.

51:37.252 --> 51:38.815
All right.

51:38.866 --> 51:40.526
I'll see you all
on Savareen.

51:40.634 --> 51:41.654
Savareen it is.

51:41.708 --> 51:43.497
- I feel great about this plan.
- Me, too.

51:43.499 --> 51:45.224
We should do this again.
It's been fun.

51:45.756 --> 51:46.273
Great.

51:46.275 --> 51:47.937
Oh, just one more thing.

51:48.509 --> 51:50.274
If you do fail me again,

51:51.916 --> 51:53.461
we'll all be out of options.

51:54.065 --> 51:55.135
Right?

51:55.137 --> 51:56.204
We won't.

51:59.239 --> 52:02.055
So, I thought
that went really well.

52:02.107 --> 52:04.347
Let's get this done as quick
and as clean as possible.

52:04.349 --> 52:05.234
What do you need?

52:05.236 --> 52:06.994
I can scrounge up
the gear.

52:06.996 --> 52:08.508
Do you got a line
on a ship?

52:08.713 --> 52:09.747
I know a guy.

52:11.004 --> 52:13.467
And I know
just where to find him.

52:13.469 --> 52:15.527
It's a long shot,
but it's worth a try.

52:15.631 --> 52:16.896
He's the best
smuggler around.

52:16.898 --> 52:18.050
He's slipped through
the Empire's fingers

52:18.052 --> 52:20.181
more times than anyone else.

52:20.653 --> 52:22.996
He's attractive, too.

52:22.998 --> 52:23.960
Sophisticated,

52:23.962 --> 52:27.764
with impeccable taste
and... Charisma.

52:29.596 --> 52:31.862
Not to mention
his prodigious...

52:31.942 --> 52:32.944
We get it.

52:37.556 --> 52:40.710
But he's retired.
Says he's a sportsman now.

52:40.712 --> 52:42.472
All we need is his ship.

52:42.587 --> 52:44.298
Well, he'll never
part with it.

52:44.300 --> 52:45.480
He loves that ship.

52:45.482 --> 52:46.949
He won it

52:47.682 --> 52:48.626
playing Sabacc.

52:48.628 --> 52:49.906
And there's the rub, right?

52:49.908 --> 52:52.020
How was I supposed to know
she was an Imperial spy?

52:52.022 --> 52:54.217
I thought she loved me.

52:54.312 --> 52:55.750
That's the guy, huh?

52:55.752 --> 52:57.113
Hmm.

52:57.610 --> 52:59.308
An interesting style.

52:59.583 --> 53:00.585
I'll say.

53:01.374 --> 53:02.506
You say he won his ship?

53:02.508 --> 53:04.623
You have an awful Sabacc face.
I'm gonna call it.

53:04.625 --> 53:06.262
I can take him.
Let me at him.

53:06.264 --> 53:07.726
Absolutely not.

53:07.728 --> 53:09.789
Han, these guys
are serious gamblers.

53:09.850 --> 53:11.946
I'm serious. Stake me.

53:11.948 --> 53:14.353
Don't listen to him.

53:20.736 --> 53:22.811
Thank you. Thank you.

53:22.813 --> 53:24.582
You see, how'd you guys
let me beat you on that one?

53:24.584 --> 53:25.585
Come on.

53:26.904 --> 53:29.020
There's no liars in this game,
just players.

53:29.143 --> 53:30.612
Is this seat taken?

53:33.596 --> 53:36.039
If nobody's in the seat,
then it ain't taken, friend.

53:39.104 --> 53:41.598
So this is, uh, Sabacc?

53:41.919 --> 53:42.752
Sabacc.

53:42.754 --> 53:45.385
Sabacc. Got it.

53:45.439 --> 53:46.633
You play it before?

53:46.914 --> 53:48.406
A couple times, yeah.

53:49.919 --> 53:51.376
Captain Lando Calrissian.

53:51.409 --> 53:53.227
Han Solo.

53:53.229 --> 53:55.157
Looks like you're
having a good day.

53:55.382 --> 53:56.436
I'm a lucky guy.

53:57.546 --> 54:00.226
Can I ask you a question,
Captain Calrissian?

54:00.437 --> 54:01.781
Anything, Han.

54:02.069 --> 54:05.450
That's "Han",
but that's okay.

54:05.452 --> 54:09.089
I heard a story about you.
I was wondering if it's true.

54:10.245 --> 54:13.845
Everything you've heard
about me is true.

54:13.992 --> 54:14.972
Thanks, love.

54:14.974 --> 54:17.302
Did you win your ship
playing cards?

54:17.304 --> 54:18.888
Oh, I've won
a lot of things.

54:20.479 --> 54:23.543
I once won a subtropical moon
in the Oseon Belt.

54:23.921 --> 54:24.748
Wow.

54:24.750 --> 54:26.876
Turned out to be
a real money pit.

54:26.954 --> 54:27.606
I'm impressed.

54:27.646 --> 54:28.908
I don't think I'd have
the nerve to gamble

54:28.910 --> 54:31.204
with something
I love as much as my ship.

54:31.248 --> 54:32.810
- Really?
- Yeah.

54:33.241 --> 54:34.275
What do you fly?

54:34.981 --> 54:36.783
VCX-100.

54:38.304 --> 54:40.208
That is a quality ship.
Right, boys?

54:40.302 --> 54:42.065
It's the fastest
in the galaxy,

54:42.067 --> 54:43.496
but there's a lot of
great ships out there.

54:43.498 --> 54:45.901
I mean, I'm sure
yours is very nice.

54:46.055 --> 54:47.924
Gets me where I'm goin'.

54:52.317 --> 54:53.551
Beginner's luck.

54:53.642 --> 54:55.444
Well played.

55:02.574 --> 55:04.570
Let's see what
we got here.

55:04.572 --> 55:06.365
Oh, great hand!

55:10.061 --> 55:13.058
Sorry, guys.
Close, but not quite.

55:22.671 --> 55:24.840
Eyes on
your own cards, buddy.

55:25.399 --> 55:27.007
All of 'em.

55:27.009 --> 55:28.933
There.
Well, now I see yours.

55:34.132 --> 55:38.371
Oh, that's me?
Okay, let's see...

55:40.938 --> 55:42.900
Sorry, minus two.

55:47.616 --> 55:49.521
This game is fun.

55:49.590 --> 55:51.536
All right,
how about this?

55:51.566 --> 55:54.200
I'll see your bet
and I'll raise you.

55:55.663 --> 55:57.799
2,000.

56:01.536 --> 56:03.109
I'll see your 2,000

56:03.504 --> 56:05.633
and I'll raise you

56:06.153 --> 56:07.772
however much this is.

56:10.579 --> 56:12.230
Whoa, whoa, whoa, Han.

56:12.292 --> 56:13.821
Slow down.

56:13.948 --> 56:15.530
You might wanna quit
while you're ahead.

56:15.604 --> 56:17.605
You might wanna quit
while you're behind.

56:19.651 --> 56:21.380
I like this kid.

56:21.452 --> 56:22.547
You're adorable.

56:22.587 --> 56:23.948
And I'm serious.

56:24.279 --> 56:25.379
And I'm calling.

56:26.027 --> 56:27.454
With what?

56:27.494 --> 56:28.488
Your scarf?

56:28.647 --> 56:29.724
Not my style.

56:29.764 --> 56:30.931
My ship.

56:32.250 --> 56:33.678
Against your ship.

56:35.626 --> 56:37.461
Time to find out
if you got the nerve.

56:40.517 --> 56:41.785
What the hell?

56:45.801 --> 56:47.066
Straight Staves.

56:56.767 --> 56:59.264
You played me.
You're good.

56:59.327 --> 57:00.936
- Yeah.
- You're very good.

57:01.532 --> 57:03.294
But not good enough.

57:03.529 --> 57:04.480
Full Sabacc.

57:11.142 --> 57:12.818
I told you to quit
while you were ahead.

57:14.906 --> 57:16.909
Drinks on me!

57:21.114 --> 57:22.514
Yeah, that's right.

57:29.694 --> 57:31.015
First of all,
there's no way

57:31.017 --> 57:32.596
he could've had
that green sylop.

57:32.598 --> 57:33.602
They'd all been played.

57:33.604 --> 57:35.332
Also, your guy,
Captain Wonderful,

57:35.337 --> 57:36.778
is so full of bantha crap...

57:36.780 --> 57:38.515
Yoo-hoo!

57:40.531 --> 57:42.366
Where's my VCX?

57:42.776 --> 57:44.391
I don't have it
right here now.

57:44.393 --> 57:45.844
It's in the shop.

57:45.846 --> 57:47.630
- I'm getting some work done.
- Lando.

57:49.460 --> 57:50.889
Qi'ra.

57:52.009 --> 57:55.105
You look phenomenal.
As always.

57:55.238 --> 57:57.106
Well, I knew I was
gonna see you.

57:57.815 --> 57:58.718
Get off!

57:58.720 --> 58:00.146
What are you doing
with hairy and the boy?

58:00.148 --> 58:02.612
- There's no need, none.
- They work for me.

58:02.710 --> 58:03.877
Good help
is hard to find, no?

58:03.879 --> 58:05.214
We're more like partners.

58:06.693 --> 58:07.818
We are.

58:08.045 --> 58:09.045
Excuse us.

58:09.959 --> 58:11.293
Listen, last I checked,

58:11.295 --> 58:12.992
me and Crimson Dawn,
we're squared away.

58:13.098 --> 58:14.759
Dryden said
all is forgiven

58:14.761 --> 58:16.968
after I did the whole
Felucia thing for him.

58:16.970 --> 58:19.773
Yeah. New move,
we're making the Kessel Run.

58:21.493 --> 58:22.754
We need a ship.

58:22.756 --> 58:24.081
Why didn't you
just say so?

58:24.083 --> 58:25.326
I thought
you were retired.

58:26.752 --> 58:28.686
Circumstances change.

58:29.145 --> 58:30.673
How much?

58:30.713 --> 58:32.165
The Kessel Run.

58:32.233 --> 58:35.003
That's no easy spin.
I'm gonna need half the take.

58:35.116 --> 58:36.455
Ridiculous.

58:36.457 --> 58:38.629
Grown-ups are talking.

58:38.860 --> 58:40.095
25%.

58:45.361 --> 58:46.628
You're Tobias Beckett.

58:47.418 --> 58:48.892
You killed Aurra Sing.

58:50.008 --> 58:52.520
Pushed her. Pretty sure
the fall killed her.

58:52.522 --> 58:55.484
You did the galaxy a favor
that day. Me, especially.

58:55.486 --> 58:56.514
I owed her
a lot of money.

58:56.516 --> 58:58.611
And as token
of my gratitude,

58:58.978 --> 59:01.262
I'm willing
to do this for 40%.

59:04.501 --> 59:05.970
25.

59:11.122 --> 59:13.084
25% works.

59:13.187 --> 59:15.596
No! Unacceptable!

59:15.754 --> 59:17.725
Stop exploiting droids!

59:17.795 --> 59:19.946
You sloppy degenerate bios!

59:20.059 --> 59:21.622
- She never learns.
- Have you no shame?

59:21.662 --> 59:22.698
Who?

59:22.750 --> 59:23.415
My first mate.

59:23.417 --> 59:25.960
You got no business
being here. Get out of here!

59:26.000 --> 59:28.878
How can you condone
this savagery?

59:28.976 --> 59:31.671
You, you. You should
not be doing this.

59:31.673 --> 59:34.311
They're using you
for entertainment.

59:34.313 --> 59:36.176
Yeah. You've
been neurowashed.

59:36.207 --> 59:38.401
Don't just blindly
follow the program.

59:38.403 --> 59:40.422
Exercise some free will!

59:41.594 --> 59:43.090
Stay away from him!

59:43.216 --> 59:44.530
He's never
had it so good.

59:44.596 --> 59:47.597
Oh, really? How about you have
a go at me, ya lumpy brute.

59:47.629 --> 59:48.689
Bring it on!
Come on!

59:48.727 --> 59:49.610
L3!

59:49.612 --> 59:51.871
Droid rights!
We are sentient!

59:51.927 --> 59:53.929
I'm gonna flip your switch.

59:54.870 --> 59:56.049
Good luck finding it.

59:56.051 --> 59:57.283
L3!

59:59.131 --> 01:00:01.060
Let go
of the mean man's face.

01:00:01.128 --> 01:00:01.933
We're leaving.

01:00:01.979 --> 01:00:04.239
They don't even
serve our kind here.

01:00:04.380 --> 01:00:05.193
Now.

01:00:09.005 --> 01:00:10.667
Who are these guys?

01:00:10.669 --> 01:00:11.845
We're taking them
to Kessel.

01:00:12.501 --> 01:00:13.653
Oh, are we?

01:00:14.326 --> 01:00:16.591
And what if I don't elect
to go to Kessel?

01:00:16.698 --> 01:00:17.897
Please don't start.

01:00:17.943 --> 01:00:19.556
Or what,
you'll have me wiped?

01:00:19.598 --> 01:00:21.895
You couldn't get from here
to Black Spire without me.

01:00:21.951 --> 01:00:23.408
Now you're gonna
make the Kessel Run?

01:00:23.462 --> 01:00:25.524
If she doesn't wanna fly,
I'll be your co-pilot.

01:00:25.564 --> 01:00:27.292
- I don't mind.
- No, no. It's okay.

01:00:27.638 --> 01:00:28.864
She's definitely going.

01:00:28.866 --> 01:00:32.097
Oh, why? Because
you're my organic overlord?

01:00:32.099 --> 01:00:34.061
Because I'm your
captain, how about that?

01:00:34.243 --> 01:00:36.605
I actually would have
her memory wiped,

01:00:36.607 --> 01:00:37.424
but she's got
the best damn

01:00:37.426 --> 01:00:39.555
navigational database
in the galaxy.

01:00:40.033 --> 01:00:41.694
Could use a fresh coat
of paint, though!

01:00:41.747 --> 01:00:46.177
Landonis, you do not want to
press that button with me.

01:00:46.369 --> 01:00:48.932
You know, a lot of
ships around here get boosted.

01:00:49.144 --> 01:00:51.386
So, I keep mine locked up.

01:00:51.421 --> 01:00:53.102
You know, for safety.

01:00:53.752 --> 01:00:55.953
L3, do you mind?

01:01:02.016 --> 01:01:03.532
Look away.

01:01:03.599 --> 01:01:05.404
I can't perform
with you looking at me.

01:01:05.590 --> 01:01:06.542
Please indulge her.

01:01:14.672 --> 01:01:16.708
I can feel you
looking at me.

01:01:21.842 --> 01:01:23.446
What are we
doing here?

01:01:23.448 --> 01:01:24.682
This guy's a hustler.

01:01:24.684 --> 01:01:26.118
I don't even think
he's got a ship.

01:01:26.120 --> 01:01:27.748
If he does, it's gonna
be a piece of junk

01:01:27.835 --> 01:01:28.741
if it's even here.

01:01:28.743 --> 01:01:31.345
There she is,
my pride and joy.

01:01:32.359 --> 01:01:33.822
<i>The Millennium Falcon.</i>

01:01:49.371 --> 01:01:51.424
Looks like you had
a little work done.

01:01:51.488 --> 01:01:53.055
Indeed I have, Han.

01:01:53.121 --> 01:01:55.552
Installed an escape pod
in the mandible notch,

01:01:55.615 --> 01:01:58.225
alluvial dampers, a wet bar.

01:01:58.353 --> 01:01:59.880
And a fortified infraction

01:01:59.882 --> 01:02:02.145
restraint on the landing gear.

01:02:02.560 --> 01:02:05.296
Looks to me like they
impounded your ship, Lando.

01:02:06.346 --> 01:02:07.876
This is unbelievable!

01:02:08.237 --> 01:02:09.422
I'm definitely
gonna have some words

01:02:09.424 --> 01:02:11.548
with someone about this.

01:02:13.284 --> 01:02:15.453
You must have experience
with these, right?

01:02:15.468 --> 01:02:16.962
Yeah, I could
take it off.

01:02:17.033 --> 01:02:18.188
Fantastic!

01:02:18.191 --> 01:02:20.157
Along with five percent
off your cut.

01:02:20.982 --> 01:02:22.869
You're down to 20.

01:02:25.503 --> 01:02:27.364
I don't like it.

01:02:27.366 --> 01:02:28.801
I don't agree with it.

01:02:29.928 --> 01:02:31.129
But I accept it.

01:02:32.624 --> 01:02:34.274
You're getting
the hang of this, Lando.

01:02:34.985 --> 01:02:36.404
Yeah.

01:02:36.406 --> 01:02:37.605
Come on, Chewie.

01:02:37.607 --> 01:02:39.813
Gonna need a little bit of
that Wookiee oomph.

01:02:41.892 --> 01:02:43.744
<i>Your plan
is underway, Enfys.</i>

01:02:43.804 --> 01:02:45.386
<i>We've attached
the homing beacon.</i>

01:02:45.388 --> 01:02:47.362
<i>They won't elude us now.</i>

01:02:47.437 --> 01:02:48.438
<i>Good.</i>

01:02:53.469 --> 01:02:57.059
<i>If they survive, they'll
bring the prize to us.</i>

01:03:13.384 --> 01:03:15.573
This is a Corellian YT-1300.

01:03:16.222 --> 01:03:18.124
Oh. You know your stuff.

01:03:18.696 --> 01:03:20.391
I've been on one before.

01:03:20.447 --> 01:03:21.451
My dad worked the line

01:03:21.453 --> 01:03:23.955
at the CEC plant
before he got laid off.

01:03:25.141 --> 01:03:26.309
He built these.

01:03:27.563 --> 01:03:29.860
He wanted
to be a pilot, but...

01:03:30.235 --> 01:03:32.237
You, uh,
close with your old man?

01:03:33.200 --> 01:03:34.362
Not really.

01:03:34.503 --> 01:03:36.533
Yeah, me neither.

01:03:36.779 --> 01:03:38.669
My mom,
on the other hand,

01:03:38.927 --> 01:03:40.878
most amazing woman
I've ever known.

01:03:44.121 --> 01:03:45.274
Excuse me.

01:03:45.314 --> 01:03:48.027
Get your presumptuous ass
out of my seat!

01:03:53.722 --> 01:03:56.685
My sacral-occipital
circuit is sticking.

01:03:56.968 --> 01:03:58.737
You're gonna have
to do that thing again later.

01:03:59.049 --> 01:04:00.657
Yeah.

01:04:00.844 --> 01:04:02.881
All right, course
to Kessel is set.

01:04:02.943 --> 01:04:04.559
Plugging coordinates
in now.

01:04:04.704 --> 01:04:06.124
Just keep your pinky
on the yoke

01:04:06.179 --> 01:04:07.362
and try not to mess
anything up.

01:04:07.402 --> 01:04:08.363
Whatever you say, my lady.

01:04:08.403 --> 01:04:09.999
Just let me know when
you're ready to jump.

01:04:10.252 --> 01:04:11.732
Ready in...

01:04:14.645 --> 01:04:15.645
Ready.

01:04:16.384 --> 01:04:18.900
It's just a simple jump to
hyperspace, and we're there.

01:04:18.902 --> 01:04:20.278
What's so tricky about that?

01:04:20.317 --> 01:04:22.690
Plenty. Can't plot
a direct course to Kessel.

01:04:22.745 --> 01:04:24.270
You have to thread through
the Si'Klaata Cluster

01:04:24.327 --> 01:04:26.790
and then pass through
The Maelstrom.

01:04:27.072 --> 01:04:28.740
You done flirting?
I'm still ready.

01:04:30.093 --> 01:04:31.794
You might wanna
buckle up, baby.

01:04:52.562 --> 01:04:53.641
Think.

01:04:53.743 --> 01:04:55.409
Do you wanna
make that move?

01:04:55.552 --> 01:04:57.850
- Do you wanna
make that move?

01:04:57.906 --> 01:04:59.766
You made that move, okay.

01:04:59.853 --> 01:05:02.616
I guess I have to
destroy that little guy.

01:05:02.656 --> 01:05:04.798
Somehow I never
get bored with winning.

01:05:06.245 --> 01:05:08.852
No, you can't wipe 'em off.
They're holograms.

01:05:09.876 --> 01:05:11.930
Hey, hey, hey!
Chewie, relax!

01:05:11.932 --> 01:05:14.082
Hey, try to compose yourself.

01:05:14.084 --> 01:05:16.462
Look. All you gotta do is
think a few moves ahead,

01:05:16.502 --> 01:05:17.797
anticipate your opponent.

01:05:17.837 --> 01:05:20.231
There's a lesson
to be learned here.

01:05:20.303 --> 01:05:21.538
Uh, you guys seen Qi'ra?

01:05:24.405 --> 01:05:26.212
People are predictable.

01:05:47.867 --> 01:05:50.128
Yeah, I had to
try one on.

01:05:50.262 --> 01:05:51.696
That's a lot of capes.

01:05:51.767 --> 01:05:53.777
Maybe too many capes.

01:05:58.176 --> 01:05:59.804
So what's the plan?

01:05:59.892 --> 01:06:01.406
Well, I thought
we'd talk a little first

01:06:01.408 --> 01:06:03.265
and then you know...

01:06:03.267 --> 01:06:05.270
- For Kessel.
- Oh.

01:06:05.363 --> 01:06:06.878
- Mmm-hmm.
- Good.

01:06:06.956 --> 01:06:08.513
Yeah? How good?

01:06:08.895 --> 01:06:09.681
Foolproof.

01:06:09.721 --> 01:06:11.481
Well, it better be.

01:06:11.742 --> 01:06:12.550
- I...
- I...

01:06:12.649 --> 01:06:13.817
- You go first.
- No.

01:06:13.857 --> 01:06:15.485
What were you gonna say?

01:06:15.611 --> 01:06:18.470
I wanna tell you
so much.

01:06:18.955 --> 01:06:20.523
And I wanna know
everything

01:06:20.564 --> 01:06:22.280
that's happened to you
since Corellia.

01:06:23.700 --> 01:06:26.274
I'm not sure
we have that kinda time.

01:06:26.422 --> 01:06:27.530
We could.

01:06:27.570 --> 01:06:29.952
We could have all the time
we want after the job.

01:06:30.030 --> 01:06:31.110
You and I.

01:06:31.574 --> 01:06:32.774
What?

01:06:33.745 --> 01:06:35.080
I want to.

01:06:35.970 --> 01:06:37.140
You want to?

01:06:37.422 --> 01:06:39.291
To tell you everything
that's happened.

01:06:40.950 --> 01:06:43.213
But I know if I do,
you won't look at me the same.

01:06:43.520 --> 01:06:45.242
The way that you're
looking at me right now.

01:06:45.359 --> 01:06:46.703
Nothing is gonna
change the way

01:06:46.705 --> 01:06:47.552
I'm looking at you
right now.

01:06:47.554 --> 01:06:50.039
You don't know that.
You don't know what I've done.

01:07:03.850 --> 01:07:05.412
Am I interrupting something?

01:07:08.089 --> 01:07:09.043
Kinda.

01:07:09.734 --> 01:07:10.578
Good.

01:07:10.588 --> 01:07:12.940
'Cause we got
a lot of work to do.

01:07:12.980 --> 01:07:14.526
You're making
a big mistake.

01:07:14.596 --> 01:07:15.656
- Oh, really?
- Which is yours to make

01:07:15.658 --> 01:07:17.879
except when you start to
interfere with my livelihood.

01:07:17.919 --> 01:07:18.946
This isn't gonna interfere
with your livelihood.

01:07:18.986 --> 01:07:19.947
Then we have a problem.

01:07:19.987 --> 01:07:22.445
You don't see it,
because you don't want to.

01:07:22.447 --> 01:07:24.085
Maybe I know her
a little better than you do.

01:07:24.484 --> 01:07:26.952
Maybe you don't know
her well enough.

01:07:27.817 --> 01:07:28.521
All right?

01:07:28.686 --> 01:07:30.090
Look.

01:07:30.761 --> 01:07:32.259
I like you, kid.

01:07:32.375 --> 01:07:34.846
We got a good thing going here.
Me, you, Chewie.

01:07:34.910 --> 01:07:35.797
- Yeah.
- Right?

01:07:35.799 --> 01:07:38.056
The makings
of a solid crew.

01:07:38.170 --> 01:07:40.231
But it does not work
with Qi'ra.

01:07:40.451 --> 01:07:42.684
It worked with Val.
You trusted her.

01:07:44.633 --> 01:07:47.388
You wanna know how I've
survived as long as I have?

01:07:48.284 --> 01:07:49.647
I trust no one.

01:07:51.150 --> 01:07:53.540
Assume everyone
will betray you

01:07:53.542 --> 01:07:55.421
and you will never
be disappointed.

01:07:56.780 --> 01:07:58.747
Sounds like
a lonely way to live.

01:07:59.642 --> 01:08:01.280
It's the only way.

01:08:08.548 --> 01:08:09.960
Dropping out
of lightspeed now.

01:08:10.044 --> 01:08:11.042
Ready to...

01:08:16.485 --> 01:08:18.452
The Akkadese Maelstrom.

01:08:20.454 --> 01:08:22.048
I'm gonna go check
on the dampers.

01:08:22.088 --> 01:08:23.017
You need anything?

01:08:23.057 --> 01:08:24.425
Equal rights?

01:08:54.696 --> 01:08:55.791
What's that sound?

01:08:56.127 --> 01:08:59.047
Carbonbergs, size of planets,
crashing into each other.

01:08:59.049 --> 01:09:01.576
Ships fly in there,
they never come out.

01:09:01.632 --> 01:09:03.625
It's ionized gas,
water vapor,

01:09:03.704 --> 01:09:05.405
possibly vacuum-breathing
life forms

01:09:05.497 --> 01:09:06.845
swirling around The Maw.

01:09:06.918 --> 01:09:08.831
Only way in or out
is this channel.

01:09:10.536 --> 01:09:12.770
So what are you gonna do
about your little problem?

01:09:13.171 --> 01:09:14.305
Problem?

01:09:14.499 --> 01:09:15.870
Uh...

01:09:16.353 --> 01:09:17.276
Well, that brand
on your wrist

01:09:17.323 --> 01:09:19.371
tells me that
you're committed.

01:09:19.411 --> 01:09:21.305
And that young male's
heart fluctuations

01:09:21.345 --> 01:09:22.712
tell me
he's in love with you.

01:09:22.782 --> 01:09:25.376
Han is not
in love with me!

01:09:26.521 --> 01:09:28.589
Oh, please. It's just us.

01:09:28.633 --> 01:09:32.198
You don't have to pretend.
I'm in the same situation.

01:09:32.308 --> 01:09:33.071
You are?

01:09:33.073 --> 01:09:34.085
I'm sure you've noticed

01:09:34.087 --> 01:09:35.558
that Lando
has feelings for me.

01:09:35.560 --> 01:09:37.095
Which makes
working together difficult

01:09:37.097 --> 01:09:39.544
because I do not feel
the same way about him.

01:09:39.546 --> 01:09:40.940
Right.

01:09:41.031 --> 01:09:42.708
Yes, yeah.

01:09:42.741 --> 01:09:44.248
Yeah, I see that.

01:09:44.334 --> 01:09:47.070
Sometimes, I think...
Maybe.

01:09:47.799 --> 01:09:49.135
But, no.

01:09:51.077 --> 01:09:52.644
We're just not compatible.

01:09:54.733 --> 01:09:56.301
How would that work?

01:09:57.136 --> 01:09:58.135
It works.

01:10:08.282 --> 01:10:10.311
This is a precision job.

01:10:10.313 --> 01:10:12.931
Thermal vault will be
on the lowest level.

01:10:13.015 --> 01:10:14.343
Down where it's warm.

01:10:14.345 --> 01:10:16.865
The only way
we're gonna pull this off

01:10:16.867 --> 01:10:19.071
is if everybody
plays their part.

01:10:19.073 --> 01:10:20.924
Stick to the plan.

01:10:20.926 --> 01:10:23.062
Do not improvise.

01:10:27.828 --> 01:10:30.001
Mining colonies
are the worst.

01:10:30.003 --> 01:10:31.620
Yeah, well, "the worst"

01:10:31.622 --> 01:10:33.266
is where the money is.

01:10:35.430 --> 01:10:37.641
All right, people.
Time to shine.

01:11:14.115 --> 01:11:15.996
It won't be for long.

01:11:15.998 --> 01:11:17.926
Shut up, the both of you.

01:11:17.928 --> 01:11:19.688
I am Oksana Floren,

01:11:19.690 --> 01:11:22.147
Deputy Assistant Administrator
to the Vice-Admiral

01:11:22.149 --> 01:11:25.000
of the Federation of
Trade Route Allocation

01:11:25.035 --> 01:11:26.513
and Monetization.

01:11:26.629 --> 01:11:29.008
Here with an offer
from his eminence,

01:11:29.010 --> 01:11:31.061
the Senior Vice-Admiral.

01:11:31.837 --> 01:11:34.699
Your spice for our
hard-working slaves.

01:11:34.778 --> 01:11:36.261
I brought you a sample.

01:11:36.354 --> 01:11:39.023
Tuul, bring forth
the merchandise.

01:12:07.844 --> 01:12:09.572
Director Tolsite
said our slaves

01:12:09.574 --> 01:12:10.765
should follow those guys

01:12:10.767 --> 01:12:12.623
to get clipped
and tagged.

01:12:12.677 --> 01:12:14.809
What are they
clipping?

01:12:14.868 --> 01:12:16.971
Mmm-hmm.

01:12:18.566 --> 01:12:20.020
He wants us
to follow him.

01:12:24.088 --> 01:12:24.815
Really?

01:12:24.817 --> 01:12:26.113
That's for that stunt
you pulled earlier,

01:12:26.115 --> 01:12:27.505
you degenerate scum.

01:12:47.032 --> 01:12:48.702
He says all systems
in this sector

01:12:48.704 --> 01:12:50.836
of the facility operate
out of this room.

01:12:50.838 --> 01:12:52.532
It's how they're able
to maintain control

01:12:52.534 --> 01:12:54.492
over so many
with so few.

01:12:58.598 --> 01:13:00.640
The director says
their reconditioning process

01:13:00.642 --> 01:13:03.031
is excruciating
but effective.

01:13:18.204 --> 01:13:20.544
He said your security attache
can wait there.

01:13:20.636 --> 01:13:22.905
"Surely, we don't need him
to negotiate."

01:13:25.600 --> 01:13:27.109
Wait there, Tuul.

01:13:27.173 --> 01:13:28.909
Try not to bother anyone.

01:13:53.774 --> 01:13:54.876
Nice!

01:13:55.545 --> 01:13:56.339
That was the uniform

01:13:56.341 --> 01:13:58.922
that would've fit me
perfectly, but it's fine.

01:14:08.367 --> 01:14:10.168
Would you mind
holding this for me?

01:14:24.597 --> 01:14:25.891
Whoa.

01:14:25.893 --> 01:14:27.803
I have never see anyone do...

01:14:27.841 --> 01:14:28.800
What was that?

01:14:28.802 --> 01:14:31.000
Teras Kasi.

01:14:32.546 --> 01:14:34.193
Dryden taught me.

01:14:38.726 --> 01:14:39.830
Ah.

01:14:39.832 --> 01:14:41.098
Well negotiated.

01:14:51.250 --> 01:14:53.419
Excuse me.
I need to use this terminal.

01:14:53.510 --> 01:14:54.511
Hello?

01:14:55.760 --> 01:14:58.283
Can you hear me? Ugh.

01:14:58.669 --> 01:15:00.346
Restraining bolts...

01:15:00.429 --> 01:15:01.638
Barbaric.

01:15:03.603 --> 01:15:05.519
Congratulations!
You're liberated. Scoot.

01:15:05.523 --> 01:15:06.551
I don't know.

01:15:06.553 --> 01:15:07.987
Free your brothers and sisters
or something.

01:15:08.024 --> 01:15:09.594
Just give me some space.

01:15:15.619 --> 01:15:16.897
I'm in!

01:15:16.899 --> 01:15:17.964
<i>Han, can you hear me?</i>

01:15:17.966 --> 01:15:19.625
I kinda need to
know which way to go here.

01:15:19.994 --> 01:15:20.852
L3?

01:15:20.892 --> 01:15:22.573
The thermal vault
is down two levels,

01:15:22.575 --> 01:15:24.589
then left, then right,
then it's the third left.

01:15:24.629 --> 01:15:27.632
Right. That's a lot of
directions, but we're on it.

01:15:34.587 --> 01:15:35.765
They're in subsector four,

01:15:35.767 --> 01:15:38.216
coming up on gate X-3-7-1-K.

01:15:38.218 --> 01:15:39.452
Overriding!

01:15:45.772 --> 01:15:46.706
Freedom.

01:16:09.371 --> 01:16:11.433
What the hell
are you guys doing up there?

01:16:11.607 --> 01:16:13.509
I created a distraction!

01:16:18.369 --> 01:16:19.621
Come on! This way!

01:16:22.126 --> 01:16:23.998
Wait! What are you doing?

01:16:24.000 --> 01:16:25.858
Come on,
we gotta get the coaxium.

01:16:28.162 --> 01:16:30.518
Hey! Remember what Beckett
said, stick to the plan.

01:16:30.520 --> 01:16:33.457
Chewie! Come on, let's go!

01:16:37.051 --> 01:16:37.829
Fine!

01:16:40.338 --> 01:16:41.406
Chewie!

01:16:44.068 --> 01:16:45.565
Here, you might need this.

01:16:50.669 --> 01:16:52.669
Hope I see you around
sometime.

01:17:08.397 --> 01:17:09.692
Han, where are you?

01:17:09.935 --> 01:17:11.528
<i>I'm on my way
to the vault.</i>

01:17:11.631 --> 01:17:12.803
<i>I lost Chewie.</i>

01:17:12.863 --> 01:17:13.878
He's dead?

01:17:13.880 --> 01:17:15.734
No, he had something
he had to do.

01:17:15.736 --> 01:17:16.996
<i>Is he coming back?</i>

01:17:17.036 --> 01:17:18.044
I don't know.

01:17:19.330 --> 01:17:21.332
Okay, they're on to us now.

01:17:31.161 --> 01:17:32.228
I'm at the vault.

01:17:40.051 --> 01:17:41.545
That's what I said!

01:17:44.860 --> 01:17:46.895
- Huh, that was impressive.
- Yeah.

01:17:47.218 --> 01:17:48.203
We're clear.

01:17:58.775 --> 01:17:59.904
Now what?

01:18:00.116 --> 01:18:01.846
<i>Han, each canister
should be equipped</i>

01:18:01.908 --> 01:18:03.106
<i>with a thermal display.</i>

01:18:03.108 --> 01:18:04.288
Yeah, I see it.

01:18:04.290 --> 01:18:07.418
If the internal temperature
reaches below 35 standard,

01:18:07.420 --> 01:18:10.550
<i>then the coaxium will
destabilize and explode.</i>

01:18:10.552 --> 01:18:13.039
Yup, I get it, guys.
It's dangerous.

01:18:21.884 --> 01:18:23.478
Okay, got it.

01:18:23.557 --> 01:18:25.291
Great. Only eleven more.

01:18:25.735 --> 01:18:26.736
Eleven?

01:18:34.264 --> 01:18:37.194
<i>The Calrissian Chronicles,
chapter five.</i>

01:18:37.390 --> 01:18:38.909
<i>continued.</i>

01:18:38.911 --> 01:18:40.970
Personally, I wasn't all that
impressed with the Sharu.

01:18:40.972 --> 01:18:43.361
No sense of humor or style.

01:18:43.363 --> 01:18:45.511
Nonetheless,
there L3 and I were

01:18:45.513 --> 01:18:47.376
deep in their sacred temple.

01:18:47.434 --> 01:18:49.228
And that's when we saw it...

01:18:51.777 --> 01:18:53.312
Always something.

01:18:55.686 --> 01:18:57.548
You guys are not gonna believe
what I'm seeing up here.

01:18:57.675 --> 01:18:59.684
<i>Is it
a mass breakout?</i>

01:19:00.161 --> 01:19:01.137
L3, what did you do?

01:19:01.139 --> 01:19:03.233
I found my true purpose,
Lando.

01:19:03.235 --> 01:19:04.551
That's what I've done.

01:19:06.203 --> 01:19:08.496
I'm so glad
we took this job!

01:19:08.498 --> 01:19:09.968
That droid!

01:19:09.970 --> 01:19:11.129
L3, come on!

01:19:14.362 --> 01:19:16.011
Follow me, compatriots!

01:19:23.281 --> 01:19:25.160
Another couple guards
just spotted me.

01:19:25.162 --> 01:19:27.112
I don't have a free hand
to take 'em out.

01:19:27.114 --> 01:19:28.834
<i>- What do I do?
- Improvise.</i>

01:19:28.890 --> 01:19:30.791
You said never improvise!

01:19:39.452 --> 01:19:40.834
Hi!

01:19:40.889 --> 01:19:41.997
Don't forget that guy!

01:19:58.229 --> 01:20:00.182
Good to see you, buddy!

01:20:00.371 --> 01:20:02.454
Stay with me, Sagwa!
Keep up!

01:20:05.826 --> 01:20:07.569
Hey! I'm Chewie's
friend, Han.

01:20:10.303 --> 01:20:11.273
Okay.

01:20:38.598 --> 01:20:40.732
Han!

01:20:42.457 --> 01:20:43.458
Hey!

01:20:54.734 --> 01:20:55.822
Follow me.

01:20:58.185 --> 01:21:00.618
Rebellion!

01:21:10.743 --> 01:21:12.258
They're going for
the landing gear!

01:21:12.260 --> 01:21:13.603
We've gotta
get out of here!

01:21:15.463 --> 01:21:17.953
We need to keep 'em away
from those cannons!

01:21:26.055 --> 01:21:27.256
Catch that!

01:21:29.753 --> 01:21:31.598
Coaxium's stowed!
Let's go!

01:21:32.038 --> 01:21:33.412
Where's L3?

01:21:33.456 --> 01:21:36.527
No more subjugation!

01:21:40.657 --> 01:21:41.964
L3!

01:21:41.973 --> 01:21:43.975
No, Lando!
Get back here!

01:21:46.631 --> 01:21:47.933
Lando!

01:21:48.987 --> 01:21:50.664
System failure.

01:21:50.666 --> 01:21:52.902
Have to reroute
the sensory modulators.

01:21:52.966 --> 01:21:54.584
It's all right.
Save your energy.

01:21:54.586 --> 01:21:56.349
I'm gonna get you outta here.
All right?

01:21:56.351 --> 01:21:57.985
System failure...

01:22:03.540 --> 01:22:04.690
Rerouting...

01:22:06.079 --> 01:22:07.372
Damn it!

01:22:07.374 --> 01:22:08.205
Han!

01:22:13.894 --> 01:22:15.227
Sagwa.

01:22:15.288 --> 01:22:16.724
This way!

01:22:17.478 --> 01:22:18.882
Come, come!

01:22:29.118 --> 01:22:30.785
Chewie!
Damn it!

01:22:34.602 --> 01:22:35.970
It's not responding.

01:22:53.236 --> 01:22:55.340
What are you
standing around for? Come on!

01:23:01.107 --> 01:23:02.666
It's okay,
you'll be fine.

01:23:04.380 --> 01:23:06.281
It's not responding...
Not responding...

01:23:06.874 --> 01:23:08.108
Han, get us out of here.

01:23:09.202 --> 01:23:09.965
It's not responding.

01:23:09.967 --> 01:23:11.328
Han! Now!

01:23:12.011 --> 01:23:13.011
On it.

01:23:41.206 --> 01:23:42.426
- Lando...
- I'm here.

01:23:42.943 --> 01:23:44.703
- It's all right, L3.
- Lando...

01:23:44.705 --> 01:23:45.856
- I've got you.
- This is not...

01:23:45.858 --> 01:23:47.416
- It's okay, L3.
- Lando.

01:23:47.418 --> 01:23:49.851
It's all right. I can fix you.
I can fix you.

01:23:50.055 --> 01:23:51.255
Lando.

01:23:51.257 --> 01:23:53.307
What's happening to me?

01:23:56.009 --> 01:23:57.243
L3?

01:23:57.943 --> 01:23:59.011
L3!

01:24:06.129 --> 01:24:08.383
I'm sorry, girl.

01:24:08.385 --> 01:24:09.987
I'm so sorry.

01:24:23.865 --> 01:24:25.168
I could use a co-pilot.

01:24:49.552 --> 01:24:50.987
Sorry.

01:24:53.833 --> 01:24:54.788
With the cargo
we're carrying,

01:24:54.790 --> 01:24:56.015
if we don't make up
some lost time

01:24:56.017 --> 01:24:58.379
we're gonna be
in real trouble.

01:24:58.501 --> 01:25:00.026
How about that?
Is that real trouble?

01:25:06.612 --> 01:25:08.985
That is an Imperial blockade.

01:25:08.987 --> 01:25:10.663
What's it doing here?

01:25:10.665 --> 01:25:12.654
Probably heard about
your little rebellion.

01:25:14.366 --> 01:25:16.196
Nope.
Not gonna make it.

01:25:16.198 --> 01:25:17.429
We're gonna have to
drop the shipment.

01:25:17.431 --> 01:25:19.944
If we don't deliver,
Dryden will kill us.

01:25:19.946 --> 01:25:21.641
All right, trust me,
I know these guys.

01:25:21.643 --> 01:25:22.906
I used to be one of 'em.

01:25:22.908 --> 01:25:24.836
There's no way they're
gonna waste a TIE fighter

01:25:24.838 --> 01:25:26.767
chasing down a little
rinky-dink freighter.

01:25:31.622 --> 01:25:32.344
You were saying?

01:25:32.346 --> 01:25:33.886
Usually,
in situations like this

01:25:33.888 --> 01:25:36.014
I like to turn around
in the opposite direction.

01:25:45.173 --> 01:25:46.675
I'm on the ventral gun.

01:25:52.043 --> 01:25:53.252
It's an easy equation.

01:25:53.254 --> 01:25:55.284
We simply don't have enough
time to get to Savareen

01:25:55.286 --> 01:25:56.506
before the canisters explode!

01:25:56.508 --> 01:25:57.882
Just have to find
a faster route.

01:25:57.884 --> 01:25:58.984
There isn't one!
You can't make

01:25:58.986 --> 01:26:00.770
the Kessel Run
in less than 20 parsecs.

01:26:00.772 --> 01:26:02.253
- Watch me.
- How?

01:26:02.309 --> 01:26:04.192
Take a shortcut,
through there.

01:26:05.120 --> 01:26:07.188
- Into The Maelstrom?
- Mmm-hmm.

01:26:07.190 --> 01:26:09.244
Spectacular way of killing
us all, I'll give you that.

01:26:09.246 --> 01:26:11.134
- Can't do it without L3.
- She's gone!

01:26:11.136 --> 01:26:12.524
You said yourself
she's got the best

01:26:12.526 --> 01:26:14.116
navigational database
in the galaxy.

01:26:14.118 --> 01:26:15.295
If we remove
her neural core,

01:26:15.297 --> 01:26:16.670
it's possible we can
download her brain

01:26:16.672 --> 01:26:18.819
<i>into the Falcon's
navicomputer, right?</i>

01:26:18.898 --> 01:26:19.899
Could we?

01:26:20.223 --> 01:26:21.454
Theoretically.

01:26:21.456 --> 01:26:23.124
Only one way to find out.

01:26:26.000 --> 01:26:27.967
I got a really good feeling
about this.

01:26:42.381 --> 01:26:43.847
Oops, that's on me.

01:26:50.934 --> 01:26:52.268
Okay.

01:26:54.377 --> 01:26:56.220
Beckett, you see them?
They still on us?

01:26:59.425 --> 01:27:00.795
<i>Beckett, did you hear me?</i>

01:27:00.797 --> 01:27:02.059
<i>Are they on us?</i>

01:27:02.061 --> 01:27:04.143
Like rashnold on a kalak.

01:27:05.024 --> 01:27:06.522
I don't know
what that means.

01:27:06.553 --> 01:27:08.782
Like a gingleson's pelt.

01:27:09.034 --> 01:27:10.755
What?
Are they or aren't they?

01:27:10.757 --> 01:27:12.570
Yes, they're still on us!

01:27:14.711 --> 01:27:15.911
Whoo!

01:27:19.271 --> 01:27:24.086
This is why you never let
anyone fly your ship.

01:27:24.124 --> 01:27:25.161
Come on!

01:27:29.434 --> 01:27:32.114
Yeah, one just got past me.
He's right on top of us!

01:27:41.746 --> 01:27:43.115
<i>Good going, Han!</i>

01:27:49.117 --> 01:27:50.396
We need to
divert auxiliary power

01:27:50.398 --> 01:27:51.649
to the rear deflector shield.

01:27:51.651 --> 01:27:54.549
We definitely do!

01:28:01.203 --> 01:28:02.976
Since when do you know
how to fly?

01:28:05.449 --> 01:28:07.112
190 years old?

01:28:08.987 --> 01:28:10.215
You look great!

01:28:11.423 --> 01:28:12.685
Chewie, get in.

01:28:12.740 --> 01:28:13.821
I'll help Lando.

01:28:28.833 --> 01:28:31.094
Whoa!
That's my cape!

01:28:31.096 --> 01:28:32.873
Ah! That's a custom piece!

01:28:40.391 --> 01:28:42.322
What? Beckett, you with us?

01:28:42.324 --> 01:28:44.678
We just lost the cannon!

01:28:44.680 --> 01:28:46.641
And I really hurt
my thumbs.

01:28:46.728 --> 01:28:48.163
<i>There's still one on us.</i>

01:28:54.172 --> 01:28:55.608
Drop the landing gear.

01:28:56.139 --> 01:28:57.610
When I tell you,
flood the intake

01:28:57.612 --> 01:28:59.145
and sweep to the bi-lats.

01:29:02.839 --> 01:29:05.488
A little something I picked up
from my pal, Needles,

01:29:05.490 --> 01:29:07.439
best street racer
in all of Corellia.

01:29:08.509 --> 01:29:09.837
Till he crashed

01:29:09.964 --> 01:29:12.295
and died, doing this.

01:29:30.123 --> 01:29:31.756
Flood it, it's all yours!

01:29:43.523 --> 01:29:45.853
Nice move!

01:29:48.865 --> 01:29:50.565
Pull out her
internal processor.

01:29:53.575 --> 01:29:54.477
Sorry.

01:30:01.061 --> 01:30:02.186
We've got L3.

01:30:04.193 --> 01:30:05.707
Remove the mod calibrator.

01:30:05.709 --> 01:30:06.770
Make sure
the T-Line's connected.

01:30:06.826 --> 01:30:08.458
I'm gonna tuck it in.
Don't worry.

01:30:08.529 --> 01:30:09.493
You close?

01:30:09.495 --> 01:30:11.958
That coaxium's
getting real ripe.

01:30:12.201 --> 01:30:14.329
Okay.

01:30:16.226 --> 01:30:17.929
She's interfacing.

01:30:22.031 --> 01:30:23.933
She's part of the ship now.

01:30:35.514 --> 01:30:36.986
Where the hell are we?

01:30:37.030 --> 01:30:38.397
We're way off
the edge of the map.

01:30:39.162 --> 01:30:40.116
Wait.

01:30:40.172 --> 01:30:42.808
L3's constructing a model
of The Maelstrom.

01:30:45.306 --> 01:30:47.707
She says we're
approaching The Maw.

01:30:47.748 --> 01:30:48.877
That doesn't
sound like something

01:30:48.879 --> 01:30:50.385
we wanna be approaching.

01:31:11.445 --> 01:31:12.388
Hang on!

01:31:18.048 --> 01:31:18.837
This is The Maw?

01:31:18.839 --> 01:31:20.882
No, that's not The Maw.
I don't know what this is.

01:31:20.884 --> 01:31:22.119
That's a living thing.

01:31:36.840 --> 01:31:38.135
There!

01:31:38.213 --> 01:31:39.313
That's The Maw.

01:31:42.312 --> 01:31:43.696
It's a gravity well.

01:31:43.916 --> 01:31:44.994
I got an idea.

01:31:46.143 --> 01:31:47.924
Don't fly toward it, Han!

01:31:55.581 --> 01:31:56.853
See if it goes for this.

01:31:56.855 --> 01:31:58.690
No, what are you doing?
That's the escape pod!

01:32:00.158 --> 01:32:01.326
I know.

01:32:04.364 --> 01:32:05.634
Then why'd you do it?

01:32:13.051 --> 01:32:14.419
That's why, baby.

01:32:23.339 --> 01:32:24.505
She found a way out.

01:32:25.253 --> 01:32:27.865
90 degrees,
to the left... ish.

01:32:27.937 --> 01:32:28.865
Left-ish.

01:32:28.952 --> 01:32:30.231
I can't.

01:32:30.270 --> 01:32:32.141
It's taking everything we got
to stay out of The Maw.

01:32:32.172 --> 01:32:33.807
It's pulling us in.
We're stuck.

01:32:37.769 --> 01:32:40.226
We have enough raw coaxium
to power a dozen destroyers.

01:32:40.282 --> 01:32:42.219
Inject it into the fuel line,
it'll blow up the ship.

01:32:42.221 --> 01:32:43.652
Not the fuel line.

01:32:43.654 --> 01:32:45.895
But if we put one drop
into the fusion reactor,

01:32:45.950 --> 01:32:46.457
it might just...

01:32:46.516 --> 01:32:47.922
Give us the kick we need.

01:32:47.963 --> 01:32:49.729
All right, I'm on it!

01:32:54.150 --> 01:32:55.911
I know, we're getting
dragged in a circle.

01:33:09.979 --> 01:33:12.217
Once we get lined up,
it's gonna be a straight shot.

01:33:12.296 --> 01:33:13.337
As soon as that
coaxium ignites,

01:33:13.363 --> 01:33:14.167
we're gonna
tear out of here

01:33:14.169 --> 01:33:15.743
and the second we're
clear of The Maelstrom,

01:33:15.745 --> 01:33:17.135
we jump to lightspeed.

01:33:21.122 --> 01:33:22.270
Beckett!

01:33:22.272 --> 01:33:23.674
Can't talk!

01:33:27.621 --> 01:33:28.655
I see it.

01:33:53.193 --> 01:33:54.133
Beckett, hurry up!

01:33:54.135 --> 01:33:56.198
We only get one shot
at this thing!

01:33:56.529 --> 01:33:58.463
Shut up
and let me do this!

01:34:06.706 --> 01:34:09.307
Beckett, I'm gonna
count you down!

01:34:10.323 --> 01:34:11.657
Three!

01:34:14.577 --> 01:34:15.611
Two!

01:34:19.698 --> 01:34:20.836
Now!

01:34:20.905 --> 01:34:21.933
Now?

01:34:22.013 --> 01:34:22.782
Now!

01:34:39.014 --> 01:34:40.783
Oh, shoot...

01:34:53.530 --> 01:34:54.980
Chewie, when I tell you,
kick out the thrusters

01:34:54.982 --> 01:34:56.716
- and jump to lightspeed.
- Wait, what are we...

01:34:56.718 --> 01:34:57.919
Remember that alley
we slipped through

01:34:57.921 --> 01:34:59.080
in the Santhe Shipyards?

01:34:59.082 --> 01:35:01.130
Yeah, I remember!
I remember it didn't work.

01:35:01.132 --> 01:35:02.433
This time it's gonna.

01:35:12.644 --> 01:35:13.645
Punch it!

01:35:24.655 --> 01:35:26.758
<i>Savareen,
this is Millennium Falcon.</i>

01:35:26.760 --> 01:35:29.662
<i>We have coaxium that needs to
be off-loaded immediately.</i>

01:35:29.664 --> 01:35:32.100
<i>Like immediately,
immediately!</i>

01:35:33.009 --> 01:35:34.337
<i>We're here now...</i>

01:35:34.596 --> 01:35:35.697
<i>...see you. I...</i>

01:36:06.676 --> 01:36:08.889
Just did the Kessel Run
in 12 parsecs.

01:36:13.131 --> 01:36:15.071
Not if you round down, buddy.

01:36:15.425 --> 01:36:16.425
Yeah.

01:36:22.488 --> 01:36:24.757
She is a hell of a ship.

01:36:33.356 --> 01:36:34.817
I hate you.

01:36:34.881 --> 01:36:36.348
I know.

01:36:38.728 --> 01:36:40.725
I'm gonna be on my ship,

01:36:40.890 --> 01:36:42.683
in my quarters,

01:36:42.685 --> 01:36:45.756
waiting for you
to bring me my share.

01:36:47.965 --> 01:36:50.401
And then I don't ever
wanna see you again.

01:36:55.016 --> 01:36:56.417
Never?

01:37:10.179 --> 01:37:12.107
Where's your boss?

01:37:12.288 --> 01:37:14.615
Oh. Don't worry.
He'll be here.

01:37:15.858 --> 01:37:16.693
Then what?

01:37:17.293 --> 01:37:20.090
Well, you delivered,

01:37:20.388 --> 01:37:22.384
so you will get paid.

01:37:22.658 --> 01:37:25.049
You can buy that ship.

01:37:25.111 --> 01:37:28.281
You know that's not
what I'm asking.

01:37:30.950 --> 01:37:32.585
It can't happen.

01:37:36.846 --> 01:37:38.230
Because you're with Dryden?

01:37:38.232 --> 01:37:41.344
I'm not with him,
but I owe him.

01:37:43.073 --> 01:37:45.109
He helped me out
of a bad situation.

01:37:46.325 --> 01:37:48.355
And how long do you have
to pay off that debt?

01:37:51.831 --> 01:37:54.433
Everyone serves
somebody, Han.

01:37:55.287 --> 01:37:57.609
Even Dryden Vos.

01:37:57.655 --> 01:38:00.430
Look, you don't want to make
an enemy of Crimson Dawn

01:38:00.432 --> 01:38:02.882
which is exactly what you
and I would both be doing

01:38:02.884 --> 01:38:04.374
if I left here with you.

01:38:04.376 --> 01:38:06.217
I'm not afraid
of Crimson Dawn.

01:38:06.219 --> 01:38:08.348
I can take care of myself.

01:38:08.587 --> 01:38:09.959
You know,
I'm not the kid you knew

01:38:09.961 --> 01:38:11.530
on Corellia anymore, Qi'ra.

01:38:11.576 --> 01:38:12.663
- No?
- No.

01:38:12.665 --> 01:38:13.732
Then who are you?

01:38:14.717 --> 01:38:16.064
I'm an outlaw.

01:38:17.967 --> 01:38:19.246
What? I'm not kidding.

01:38:19.339 --> 01:38:20.555
Okay.

01:38:20.557 --> 01:38:23.448
Okay, outlaw,
you can tell yourself that,

01:38:23.597 --> 01:38:25.803
but I might be the only person
in the whole galaxy

01:38:25.805 --> 01:38:27.350
who knows
what you really are.

01:38:27.352 --> 01:38:29.247
Yeah.

01:38:29.249 --> 01:38:30.584
What's that?

01:38:32.991 --> 01:38:34.494
You are the good guy.

01:38:36.681 --> 01:38:39.443
I am not the good guy.

01:38:39.445 --> 01:38:43.109
I am definitely
not a good guy.

01:38:43.351 --> 01:38:44.782
I'm a terrible person.

01:38:45.329 --> 01:38:46.705
Hey!

01:38:46.707 --> 01:38:48.293
They say when
the coaxium's refined,

01:38:48.295 --> 01:38:49.842
we collect it up there.

01:39:14.375 --> 01:39:16.468
So, I hear
you make good brandy.

01:39:19.885 --> 01:39:21.320
<i>Beckett.</i>

01:39:46.043 --> 01:39:47.111
Don't.

01:39:48.489 --> 01:39:51.049
<i>You must've known
you'd see me again.</i>

01:39:51.051 --> 01:39:52.579
I was counting on it.

01:39:52.581 --> 01:39:54.895
Just didn't plan on it
being so soon.

01:39:56.045 --> 01:39:57.878
Of course now,
you've got a problem.

01:39:57.922 --> 01:39:59.824
Big problem.

01:40:03.555 --> 01:40:06.051
You happen to notice
that freighter down there?

01:40:06.192 --> 01:40:08.259
You know what's on it?

01:40:08.307 --> 01:40:10.153
About 30 hired guns.

01:40:10.155 --> 01:40:12.367
All I gotta do
is give 'em the signal,

01:40:12.369 --> 01:40:13.604
you're surrounded.

01:40:29.653 --> 01:40:31.655
Sorry.
You do your thing.

01:40:32.986 --> 01:40:35.330
By the time that coaxium
gets refined,

01:40:35.332 --> 01:40:37.131
Crimson Dawn will be here,

01:40:37.133 --> 01:40:39.136
so you go ahead
and kill us.

01:40:39.138 --> 01:40:41.033
They're gonna kill you.

01:40:41.035 --> 01:40:42.464
Perhaps
there's a compromise,

01:40:42.466 --> 01:40:44.256
one that doesn't involve
so much killing.

01:40:44.455 --> 01:40:46.619
They're marauders.

01:40:46.621 --> 01:40:48.757
They don't care
about anybody.

01:40:49.665 --> 01:40:51.566
All they know
how to do is kill.

01:41:15.069 --> 01:41:16.503
I need a drink.

01:41:16.991 --> 01:41:18.527
Bring them inside.

01:41:30.589 --> 01:41:32.524
My mother once told me

01:41:32.526 --> 01:41:33.884
about a band of mercenaries

01:41:33.886 --> 01:41:36.215
that came
to a peaceful planet.

01:41:36.408 --> 01:41:39.637
They had a resource there
these men coveted,

01:41:39.911 --> 01:41:41.774
so they took it.

01:41:41.860 --> 01:41:45.173
They kept coming back,
taking more.

01:41:45.175 --> 01:41:47.803
Until finally,
the people resisted.

01:41:48.084 --> 01:41:49.844
When they returned
demanding their tribute,

01:41:49.846 --> 01:41:53.509
the people shouted back
in one voice, "No more!"

01:41:53.797 --> 01:41:56.061
The mercenaries didn't like
the sound of that,

01:41:56.195 --> 01:41:57.092
so they cut off the tongue

01:41:57.094 --> 01:42:00.825
of every last man,
woman, and child.

01:42:01.235 --> 01:42:03.003
Do you know what
that pack of animals became?

01:42:04.688 --> 01:42:05.688
Tell them.

01:42:17.279 --> 01:42:19.140
Crimson Dawn and the rest
of the five Syndicates

01:42:19.142 --> 01:42:20.673
have committed
unspeakable crimes

01:42:20.675 --> 01:42:21.881
across the galaxy.

01:42:23.493 --> 01:42:25.082
Says you.

01:42:25.146 --> 01:42:26.175
No.

01:42:26.296 --> 01:42:28.167
Says them.

01:42:28.169 --> 01:42:30.224
Each of our worlds
has been brutalized

01:42:30.226 --> 01:42:32.017
by the Syndicates.

01:42:32.019 --> 01:42:33.635
Crimson Dawn
will use their profits

01:42:33.637 --> 01:42:34.854
from the coaxium you stole

01:42:34.856 --> 01:42:37.312
to tyrannize
system after system

01:42:37.387 --> 01:42:39.482
in league with the Empire.

01:42:39.484 --> 01:42:41.504
And what would you
use it for?

01:42:42.312 --> 01:42:44.074
The same thing my mother
would have used it for

01:42:44.076 --> 01:42:46.612
if she had survived
and still wore the mask.

01:42:48.056 --> 01:42:49.284
To fight back.

01:42:50.653 --> 01:42:52.848
We're not marauders.

01:42:53.076 --> 01:42:54.811
We're allies

01:42:55.509 --> 01:42:57.313
and the war
has just begun.

01:43:13.307 --> 01:43:16.602
You know we can't give
the coaxium to Dryden Vos.

01:43:16.712 --> 01:43:18.726
Joining the cause,
Han Solo?

01:43:18.728 --> 01:43:21.122
Just trying
to make it out alive.

01:43:21.291 --> 01:43:22.295
Got a plan?

01:43:22.297 --> 01:43:23.791
Yeah, beginning of one.

01:43:23.903 --> 01:43:24.491
Way to get our money

01:43:24.493 --> 01:43:25.378
and get out from
under the thumb

01:43:25.380 --> 01:43:27.674
of Crimson Dawn
at the same time.

01:43:27.720 --> 01:43:30.239
Maybe get your girlfriend back
while we're at it.

01:43:31.059 --> 01:43:33.850
You don't tangle
with Dryden.

01:43:33.852 --> 01:43:37.181
Because unlike us,
he actually does travel

01:43:37.260 --> 01:43:39.943
with hired guns,
his own private army.

01:43:40.438 --> 01:43:42.000
So does Enfys.

01:43:42.133 --> 01:43:44.369
Listen, here's what
I got so far.

01:43:46.416 --> 01:43:48.282
What do you think
they're saying?

01:43:51.806 --> 01:43:53.439
He's gonna try to help you.

01:43:59.256 --> 01:44:00.891
I see.

01:44:02.167 --> 01:44:05.893
Lot of ways it could go south,
and only one where it doesn't.

01:44:05.895 --> 01:44:08.397
That's why I need my partner.

01:44:12.650 --> 01:44:14.483
Not this time.

01:44:14.786 --> 01:44:16.281
I'm leaving.

01:44:16.283 --> 01:44:18.413
If you're smart,
you'll come with me.

01:44:18.549 --> 01:44:20.677
I thought you didn't
believe in running.

01:44:20.708 --> 01:44:22.944
I prefer it to dying.

01:44:50.410 --> 01:44:53.007
If by some miracle
you make it out of here,

01:44:53.110 --> 01:44:54.611
find me on Tatooine.

01:44:55.439 --> 01:44:57.368
What's on Tatooine?

01:44:57.370 --> 01:44:58.407
Heard about a job,

01:44:58.409 --> 01:45:01.238
big shot gangster
putting together a crew.

01:45:01.652 --> 01:45:03.380
That'll be the one.

01:45:03.500 --> 01:45:04.358
The one?

01:45:04.360 --> 01:45:06.557
My last score.

01:45:06.701 --> 01:45:08.262
Yeah, I still got
some debts to pay

01:45:08.264 --> 01:45:10.865
before I can head back
to Glee Anselm

01:45:11.554 --> 01:45:13.555
and get into the valachord.

01:45:46.922 --> 01:45:48.200
Welcome home.

01:45:48.202 --> 01:45:50.099
He's waiting for you.

01:45:50.194 --> 01:45:51.194
Thanks, Toht.

01:45:53.148 --> 01:45:54.634
Weapons.

01:45:54.636 --> 01:45:55.937
I didn't bring 'em.

01:45:57.576 --> 01:45:58.942
They're fine.

01:46:03.296 --> 01:46:05.099
We're gonna win.

01:46:08.147 --> 01:46:10.444
It's not that kind
of game, Han.

01:46:11.586 --> 01:46:12.791
The object isn't to win.

01:46:12.793 --> 01:46:14.944
It's just to stay in it
as long as you can.

01:46:18.096 --> 01:46:19.565
You don't know everything.

01:46:20.607 --> 01:46:21.808
No.

01:46:24.103 --> 01:46:26.421
Just a bit more than you.

01:46:34.546 --> 01:46:35.534
I knew it!

01:46:36.327 --> 01:46:37.371
My men, they all said,

01:46:37.373 --> 01:46:39.727
"There's no way
they pull this off."

01:46:39.729 --> 01:46:41.411
"Qi'ra's not ready."
That's what they said,

01:46:41.413 --> 01:46:43.547
but I had faith anyway.

01:46:45.533 --> 01:46:46.802
Where's Beckett?

01:46:46.962 --> 01:46:48.264
Beckett didn't make it.

01:46:52.347 --> 01:46:53.212
Tell me.

01:46:53.214 --> 01:46:55.643
Job took a bad turn
on Kessel.

01:46:56.035 --> 01:46:57.856
He died saving my life.

01:46:58.013 --> 01:47:00.002
How are you holding up?
You all right?

01:47:00.091 --> 01:47:00.760
I'm okay.

01:47:00.762 --> 01:47:02.456
All right, good.

01:47:02.747 --> 01:47:04.459
Colo claw fish, anyone?

01:47:04.461 --> 01:47:05.828
- No. Thank you.
- No?

01:47:05.830 --> 01:47:08.423
You know, whatever Beckett's
shortcomings may have been,

01:47:08.425 --> 01:47:09.442
I always admired him.

01:47:09.444 --> 01:47:11.210
He was a man of principles.

01:47:11.212 --> 01:47:13.673
When he made a commitment,
he honored it

01:47:13.675 --> 01:47:15.996
and I think we can
all take solace

01:47:15.998 --> 01:47:18.472
in knowing how proud
he would've been

01:47:18.474 --> 01:47:22.048
to see you here,
following his example.

01:47:22.108 --> 01:47:23.758
Han and Chewbacca
behaved admirably.

01:47:23.760 --> 01:47:25.221
They'll make
reliable smugglers,

01:47:25.223 --> 01:47:26.552
should we ever
have the need

01:47:26.554 --> 01:47:28.340
when they get
their own ship.

01:47:28.342 --> 01:47:30.710
Qi'ra.
Come here.

01:47:32.654 --> 01:47:34.407
We'd really appreciate
the opportunity

01:47:34.409 --> 01:47:36.165
to work for you again, sir.

01:47:36.167 --> 01:47:37.558
I would've been
inconsolable

01:47:37.560 --> 01:47:39.401
if anything had
happened to you, my dear.

01:47:40.683 --> 01:47:42.813
I have no one else
in my life

01:47:43.204 --> 01:47:45.806
that I trust in the way
that I trust you.

01:47:49.534 --> 01:47:52.605
Well, I guess we'll just
take our payment

01:47:52.607 --> 01:47:53.399
and get going.

01:47:53.401 --> 01:47:54.523
I'm sure you've got
competitors to crush...

01:47:54.525 --> 01:47:55.691
What?

01:47:55.693 --> 01:47:57.202
...and black markets
to dominate.

01:47:57.204 --> 01:47:59.568
Oh. Show me what
you've brought me first.

01:48:00.281 --> 01:48:02.440
You want me to open it?

01:48:02.442 --> 01:48:04.478
Oh, yes, Han.
I really do.

01:48:31.049 --> 01:48:32.408
Bring me one.

01:48:32.410 --> 01:48:34.868
I don't think
that's a good idea, Dryden.

01:48:34.870 --> 01:48:37.266
It's very explosive stuff.

01:48:37.817 --> 01:48:40.048
I never ask
for anything twice, Han.

01:49:00.738 --> 01:49:02.206
Careful.

01:49:06.277 --> 01:49:08.111
It's magnificent.

01:49:08.690 --> 01:49:09.919
How'd you do it?

01:49:10.037 --> 01:49:10.876
Wasn't easy.

01:49:10.878 --> 01:49:11.871
No, I mean,
how'd you do it?

01:49:11.873 --> 01:49:14.970
It looks exactly
like the real thing.

01:49:15.943 --> 01:49:17.900
That's 'cause it is
the real thing.

01:49:17.954 --> 01:49:18.626
Yes, and I'm saying

01:49:18.628 --> 01:49:20.784
I would believe you.
It's that good.

01:49:20.852 --> 01:49:22.615
But my associate
already told me

01:49:22.617 --> 01:49:25.470
about your plan to rob me
of my money

01:49:25.519 --> 01:49:28.283
and give the real coaxium
to Enfys Nest.

01:49:28.285 --> 01:49:29.991
Dryden, I don't know
what you're thinking

01:49:29.993 --> 01:49:31.541
or what Qi'ra
may have told you...

01:49:31.543 --> 01:49:33.925
No, not Qi'ra.
Not Qi'ra.

01:49:33.927 --> 01:49:35.219
Qi'ra, it turns out

01:49:35.284 --> 01:49:36.904
has a weak spot for you,

01:49:36.906 --> 01:49:38.735
and we'll deal
with that later.

01:49:38.737 --> 01:49:42.699
No, I'm talking about
my other associate.

01:49:42.739 --> 01:49:44.741
Can you come in
and join us, please?

01:49:56.621 --> 01:49:59.756
I am sorry, kid.

01:50:02.925 --> 01:50:04.287
Why?

01:50:04.625 --> 01:50:05.453
Come on.

01:50:05.493 --> 01:50:07.489
Don't look at me like that.

01:50:07.529 --> 01:50:08.519
You weren't paying attention.

01:50:08.521 --> 01:50:11.283
I told you,
"Don't trust anybody."

01:50:12.250 --> 01:50:14.420
Am I wrong about that?

01:50:16.858 --> 01:50:18.005
Uh-uh-uh.

01:50:18.621 --> 01:50:20.366
Back away from that.

01:50:20.368 --> 01:50:22.262
Put your paws
where I can see 'em.

01:50:22.400 --> 01:50:24.235
Check that lid.

01:50:26.380 --> 01:50:27.743
Clever.

01:50:27.967 --> 01:50:29.679
It's too late.

01:50:29.719 --> 01:50:32.111
Coaxium's refined,
and Enfys has it.

01:50:32.113 --> 01:50:34.449
Well, we figured that.

01:50:48.652 --> 01:50:50.406
Drop your weapons.

01:50:54.004 --> 01:50:56.909
<i>It's over.
We got them.</i>

01:50:57.067 --> 01:50:58.238
And there we have it.

01:50:58.240 --> 01:51:00.174
Excellent work,
Aemon, thank you.

01:51:00.176 --> 01:51:01.896
Qi'ra, help me.

01:51:04.241 --> 01:51:05.575
Tell me what to do.

01:51:06.644 --> 01:51:08.394
What would you do

01:51:08.482 --> 01:51:12.520
if the person you most
trusted in the world

01:51:13.094 --> 01:51:14.562
betrayed you?

01:51:17.314 --> 01:51:18.726
I would want
to know why.

01:51:20.940 --> 01:51:23.102
If it was
a moment of weakness

01:51:23.273 --> 01:51:24.279
or something else.

01:51:24.328 --> 01:51:25.330
And then what?

01:51:26.874 --> 01:51:29.903
And then,
I would ask that person

01:51:29.943 --> 01:51:32.196
to prove their loyalty

01:51:32.198 --> 01:51:35.935
by sacrificing
something they love.

01:51:44.358 --> 01:51:46.489
I tried to warn you
about her.

01:51:46.755 --> 01:51:49.233
You know, you're wrong
about one thing.

01:51:49.362 --> 01:51:50.622
What?

01:51:50.662 --> 01:51:52.959
I was paying attention.

01:51:52.999 --> 01:51:55.266
You told Chewie
people are predictable.

01:51:57.803 --> 01:51:59.905
You're no exception.

01:52:05.564 --> 01:52:06.693
It's empty.

01:52:06.757 --> 01:52:08.200
<i>The case is empty.</i>

01:52:08.202 --> 01:52:10.611
Aemon, what's going on?
What's happening there?

01:52:10.613 --> 01:52:12.149
Aemon?

01:52:12.212 --> 01:52:13.179
Talk to me.

01:52:39.153 --> 01:52:41.883
I hope you didn't send
all your fancy enforcers

01:52:41.885 --> 01:52:43.583
because that would leave you

01:52:43.585 --> 01:52:46.038
a little shorthanded
around here.

01:52:46.993 --> 01:52:48.432
So,

01:52:48.434 --> 01:52:52.887
if that case is empty,
then the real coaxium...

01:52:52.967 --> 01:52:54.835
Leaves here
with one of us.

01:52:59.901 --> 01:53:01.278
Beckett,
what are you doing?

01:53:01.280 --> 01:53:02.328
Thinking.

01:53:02.380 --> 01:53:03.728
And I prefer to be
the only one

01:53:03.795 --> 01:53:05.619
holding a blaster
while I'm doing it.

01:53:05.667 --> 01:53:07.271
Han, grab that coaxium,

01:53:07.273 --> 01:53:08.570
put it in the case.

01:53:08.572 --> 01:53:10.346
Big stuff,
you're coming with me.

01:53:12.054 --> 01:53:13.395
Don't do this,
Beckett.

01:53:13.397 --> 01:53:15.191
- We had a deal.
- Yeah.

01:53:15.193 --> 01:53:16.043
I'm sorry,

01:53:16.123 --> 01:53:17.685
but I'm also an entrepreneur.

01:53:17.687 --> 01:53:20.268
I mean, you of all people
understand that.

01:53:20.522 --> 01:53:21.491
Come on, let's go.

01:53:22.729 --> 01:53:24.386
You're making
a huge mistake.

01:53:24.469 --> 01:53:25.731
Won't be my first.

01:53:25.789 --> 01:53:27.361
It's gonna be your last.

01:53:27.623 --> 01:53:28.791
Maybe.

01:53:29.725 --> 01:53:31.131
Why you gotta be
so negative?

01:53:43.938 --> 01:53:45.256
Han,

01:53:45.258 --> 01:53:46.609
now's as good a time as any

01:53:46.611 --> 01:53:48.704
to reevaluate
our relationship.

01:53:49.224 --> 01:53:50.215
How so?

01:53:50.899 --> 01:53:52.846
I was just thinking,

01:53:52.848 --> 01:53:55.845
why don't we join forces
and go get Beckett together?

01:53:55.847 --> 01:53:58.717
That is a great idea.
Let's do it. You go first.

01:54:00.192 --> 01:54:01.993
Oh, Han.

01:54:28.661 --> 01:54:31.021
You can't win, Han,
and even if you could,

01:54:31.080 --> 01:54:32.287
you'd spend
the rest of your life

01:54:32.289 --> 01:54:33.601
looking over your shoulder.

01:54:34.691 --> 01:54:35.691
You know what?

01:54:36.667 --> 01:54:38.623
I'm kind of getting
used to the idea.

01:54:45.988 --> 01:54:47.582
I'm sorry.

01:54:47.654 --> 01:54:49.062
Han, she's done things that

01:54:49.064 --> 01:54:51.861
you could never understand,
but I do.

01:54:52.571 --> 01:54:54.539
I understand her completely.

01:54:55.426 --> 01:54:57.800
Once you're a part
of Crimson Dawn,

01:54:57.949 --> 01:54:59.604
you can't leave.

01:54:59.644 --> 01:55:01.347
It's not true.

01:55:01.448 --> 01:55:02.875
I know you.

01:55:03.080 --> 01:55:05.184
It's what I was taught.

01:55:05.186 --> 01:55:07.074
Find your
opponent's weakness,

01:55:07.185 --> 01:55:08.478
and use it,

01:55:08.518 --> 01:55:10.621
and today...

01:55:12.618 --> 01:55:13.956
I'm yours.

01:55:40.192 --> 01:55:41.659
I had to.

01:55:42.256 --> 01:55:44.317
Yeah.
No, I mean, you did...

01:55:44.998 --> 01:55:46.934
You did.

01:55:49.044 --> 01:55:51.201
Beckett and Chewbacca,
you have to go after them.

01:55:51.261 --> 01:55:52.456
What are you gonna do?

01:55:52.458 --> 01:55:55.219
Well, if we give
all the coaxium to Enfys,

01:55:55.324 --> 01:55:57.995
we're gonna need something
to buy our ship with.

01:56:11.753 --> 01:56:14.382
- Qi'ra...
- Go and save Chewbacca.

01:56:14.430 --> 01:56:17.500
He needs you and you're
gonna need him, too.

01:56:23.964 --> 01:56:24.965
Smile.

01:56:27.818 --> 01:56:29.099
That's the word.

01:56:30.257 --> 01:56:31.410
Whenever I imagined myself

01:56:31.412 --> 01:56:33.348
off with you
on some adventure...

01:56:34.791 --> 01:56:36.858
Always makes me smile.

01:56:44.333 --> 01:56:46.168
Go. I'm right behind you.

01:57:38.030 --> 01:57:39.341
<i>Yes?</i>

01:57:39.343 --> 01:57:42.740
I regret to inform you
that Dryden Vos is dead,

01:57:42.994 --> 01:57:44.708
murdered by the thief
he hired

01:57:44.710 --> 01:57:46.313
to steal
the coaxium shipment,

01:57:46.315 --> 01:57:47.577
his friend,

01:57:47.776 --> 01:57:49.637
Tobias Beckett.

01:57:49.972 --> 01:57:51.753
<i>Is that so?</i>

01:57:52.541 --> 01:57:55.770
<i>Where is the shipment now?</i>

01:57:56.147 --> 01:57:57.309
Gone.

01:57:57.349 --> 01:57:58.346
Beckett took it.

01:57:58.424 --> 01:58:01.060
Slaughtered the others.
I alone survived.

01:58:03.844 --> 01:58:07.077
<i>One man couldn't have
done this alone.</i>

01:58:07.930 --> 01:58:09.645
I wasn't there,

01:58:09.647 --> 01:58:12.281
but if I had been, perhaps
I could have saved him.

01:58:20.510 --> 01:58:23.940
<i>Bring the ship and
come to me on Dathomir</i>

01:58:23.942 --> 01:58:25.972
<i>and you and I
will then decide</i>

01:58:25.974 --> 01:58:28.767
<i>what to do about
the traitor, Beckett,</i>

01:58:28.823 --> 01:58:31.257
<i>and his accomplices.</i>

01:58:33.386 --> 01:58:34.521
I'm on my way.

01:58:37.103 --> 01:58:38.332
<i>Qi'ra,</i>

01:58:38.334 --> 01:58:39.662
<i>you and I</i>

01:58:39.664 --> 01:58:42.965
<i>will be working
much more closely</i>

01:58:43.074 --> 01:58:45.042
<i>from now on.</i>

01:59:15.139 --> 01:59:17.268
You're relentless.
I'll give you that.

01:59:18.666 --> 01:59:20.768
Came as fast
as I could, buddy.

01:59:21.272 --> 01:59:22.673
Dryden dead?

01:59:24.683 --> 01:59:26.516
Qi'ra kill him?

01:59:28.305 --> 01:59:30.868
Still don't get it,
do you, kid?

01:59:31.118 --> 01:59:33.352
It was never about you.

01:59:33.622 --> 01:59:35.190
She's a survivor.

01:59:36.357 --> 01:59:37.913
You know what
your problem is?

01:59:37.915 --> 01:59:39.983
You think
everybody's like you.

01:59:40.753 --> 01:59:42.439
Not you, kid.

01:59:42.441 --> 01:59:43.877
You're nothing like me.

01:59:45.884 --> 01:59:47.522
I hope you're still
paying attention

01:59:47.524 --> 01:59:49.600
because now I'm gonna tell
you the most important...

02:00:04.767 --> 02:00:07.215
You made
the smart move, kid.

02:00:07.217 --> 02:00:08.773
For once.

02:00:10.181 --> 02:00:11.781
I woulda killed you.

02:00:19.129 --> 02:00:24.043
I really was gonna
learn to play that valachord.

02:00:24.160 --> 02:00:25.361
I know.

02:02:18.533 --> 02:02:20.013
That's it.
It's all loaded.

02:02:24.024 --> 02:02:25.619
Do you know
what that really is?

02:02:25.682 --> 02:02:26.597
Yeah.

02:02:26.599 --> 02:02:29.584
About 60 million credits
worth of refined coaxium.

02:02:29.586 --> 02:02:30.897
No.

02:02:30.899 --> 02:02:33.336
It's the blood that brings
life to something new.

02:02:33.579 --> 02:02:35.680
Yeah, what?

02:02:35.682 --> 02:02:36.717
A rebellion.

02:02:37.917 --> 02:02:39.734
You could come with us,
you know.

02:02:39.736 --> 02:02:42.065
We need warriors
and leaders like you.

02:02:48.617 --> 02:02:50.781
Maybe someday
you'll feel different.

02:02:51.172 --> 02:02:53.440
Don't hold your breath, kid.

02:03:08.209 --> 02:03:09.395
Don't lose that.

02:03:21.322 --> 02:03:23.283
Very few people
have actually seen

02:03:23.442 --> 02:03:24.792
the StarCave Nebula.

02:03:24.862 --> 02:03:26.161
It's breathtaking.

02:03:26.186 --> 02:03:27.671
Not unlike your eyes.

02:03:27.829 --> 02:03:29.901
How much do you know about
intertwined celestial bodies?

02:03:29.903 --> 02:03:32.121
Because I happen to be
something of an authority.

02:03:33.073 --> 02:03:34.325
By the way...

02:03:40.572 --> 02:03:42.001
Han!

02:03:42.119 --> 02:03:43.253
You're alive!

02:03:43.255 --> 02:03:44.581
Yeah, no thanks to you.

02:03:44.583 --> 02:03:46.347
I should have Chewie
rip your arms off.

02:03:46.349 --> 02:03:47.877
In fact, Chewie, do it.

02:03:47.879 --> 02:03:49.053
Hey, Han!
We are friends.

02:03:49.055 --> 02:03:50.769
You know that.
We're friends. All right?

02:03:55.967 --> 02:03:57.842
Oh, look at you.

02:03:57.844 --> 02:03:59.736
Thought he was gonna
rip your arms off.

02:03:59.857 --> 02:04:00.814
I knew you were kidding.

02:04:00.816 --> 02:04:01.660
No, you didn't.

02:04:01.662 --> 02:04:03.483
- So, where's my cut?
- Your cut?

02:04:04.589 --> 02:04:06.805
No, I don't think so.
We barely made it out alive.

02:04:06.807 --> 02:04:08.608
All we ended up with
was that.

02:04:09.400 --> 02:04:11.028
Mmm-mmm.

02:04:11.030 --> 02:04:12.553
Figure it's worth
about 10,000,

02:04:12.555 --> 02:04:14.276
maybe enough
for a decent buy-in.

02:04:16.397 --> 02:04:17.832
You want a rematch?

02:04:19.202 --> 02:04:20.471
Why not?

02:04:24.378 --> 02:04:26.339
You fold now,

02:04:26.409 --> 02:04:27.284
you walk away with enough

02:04:27.286 --> 02:04:29.381
to get yourself
your own little ship.

02:04:29.997 --> 02:04:31.300
You call,

02:04:32.395 --> 02:04:34.100
I'm gonna
clean you out again.

02:04:46.625 --> 02:04:47.950
I don't know,
I'm feeling lucky.

02:04:50.162 --> 02:04:52.758
Ooh.

02:04:52.876 --> 02:04:55.239
<i>You really have it bad
for the Falcon, don't you?</i>

02:04:55.311 --> 02:04:57.940
It's mutual, trust me.
She belongs with me.

02:05:07.590 --> 02:05:10.085
You got everything
you need there, pal?

02:05:19.906 --> 02:05:21.375
Not bad.

02:05:21.750 --> 02:05:24.391
Not bad. You know,

02:05:24.393 --> 02:05:28.237
if you'd only had
this little green sylop,

02:05:28.239 --> 02:05:29.735
you would've beaten this.

02:05:35.586 --> 02:05:38.553
Fair and square, baby.
Fair and square.

02:05:49.247 --> 02:05:50.775
Beckett said
he heard about this

02:05:50.777 --> 02:05:53.065
very big gangster
putting together a job.

02:05:53.854 --> 02:05:56.021
No, I'm telling ya,

02:05:56.102 --> 02:05:57.390
it's gonna be great.

02:05:57.503 --> 02:05:59.373
When have I ever
steered you wrong?

02:06:09.389 --> 02:06:14.393
Subtitles by explosiveskull
